module
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.QuasiCompact
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.QuasiCompact.LocallySurjectiveTransfer
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Density
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.LocallyBijective
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.GlobalSections
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Sections of a filtered colimit of sheaves of sets

Let `C` be a site, let `F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)` be a filtered diagram of sheaves of sets
and let `U` be an object of `C`. Taking sections over `U` does not in general commute with the
colimit: a colimit of sheaves is the sheafification of the colimit of the underlying presheaves,
so the canonical map
`Ψ : colim_i F_i(U) ⟶ (colim_i F_i)(U)`
need be neither injective nor surjective. It is injective as soon as the transition maps of the
diagram are injective, and also as soon as `U` is quasi-compact as an object of the site
(Stacks 090H); it is bijective under either of two combinations of those hypotheses.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_sheafSections`: the four parts of
  Stacks 0738, in order, as the four conjuncts of one statement:
  (1) `Ψ` is injective when every transition map is a monomorphism;
  (2) `Ψ` is injective when `U` is quasi-compact;
  (3) `Ψ` is bijective when both hold;
  (4) `Ψ` is bijective when the coverings of `U` by finite families whose pairwise fibre products
  are quasi-compact are cofinal among the coverings of `U`.

## Implementation notes

`Ψ` is `CategoryTheory.Limits.colimit.post F G` for the sections functor
`G = (sheafSections J _).obj (op U)`: the map out of `colim_i F_i(U)` induced by the images under
`G` of the components of the colimit cocone of `F`. That is the map of the source, and the
statement is about it rather than about the existence of some comparison map. The colimit is
formed in `Sheaf J (Type max u v)`, not in presheaves; it exists for every diagram because
sheafification of `Type max u v`-valued presheaves on a `Category.{v} C` with `C : Type u` does,
so the only smallness hypothesis is `HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)`, which is what makes
the source of `Ψ` exist.

Filteredness of `I` is used by every part: parts (2)-(4) choose an index dominating a finite set
of indices, and part (1) needs `V ↦ colim_i F_i(V)` to be a presheaf whose colimit is filtered in
order for injective transition maps to make it separated. Each conjunct carries exactly the
hypotheses of the corresponding part of the source and no others, so no part is a decorated
special case of another: (1) constrains the diagram only, (2) constrains `U` only, and (3), (4)
are the two ways the source gets surjectivity.

Points where the form departs from the wording of the source, none of them weakenings:

* "the transition maps are injective" is `Mono (F.map f)` for every morphism `f` of the index
  category. For sheaves of sets this is exactly injectivity on sections over every object of `C`
  (`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.Hom.mono_iff_presheaf_mono` and
  `CategoryTheory.NatTrans.mono_iff_mono_app`), and it is the spelling that does not name a
  choice of test object.
* "`Ψ` is an isomorphism" (part (3)) and "`Ψ` is bijective" (part (4)) are both
  `Function.Bijective`: in `Type max u v` the isomorphisms are the bijections.
* A family of morphisms with fixed target `{U_j ⟶ U}_{j ∈ J}` is a
  `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover U`, it is a covering when its generated sieve `sieve₀` lies
  in `J U`, and it refines a covering sieve `S` when `sieve₀ ≤ S`. So "`U` has a cofinal system
  of coverings of the given kind" is "every covering sieve of `U` contains the sieve generated by
  such a family", which is how the hypothesis is used: it refines the covering on which a given
  section of the target is locally in the image.
* Quasi-compactness of `U_j ×_U U_{j'}` is stated as: some fibre product of `U_j ⟶ U` and
  `U_{j'} ⟶ U` exists and is quasi-compact. Asserting existence keeps the hypothesis as strong as
  the source's, where the fibre products of the members of a covering are part of the data of a
  site (Stacks 00VH (3)), and avoids imposing `Limits.HasPullbacks C` on the whole statement.
* Quasi-compactness of an object of the site is `GrothendieckTopology.IsQuasiCompactObject`
  (Stacks 090H). Mathlib's `QuasiCompact` predicates concern schemes and are unrelated.

The hypotheses are satisfiable: for the trivial topology `⊥` every presheaf is a sheaf and every
object is quasi-compact (`GrothendieckTopology.isQuasiCompactObject_bot`), so (2) and (3) apply
there to any filtered diagram of presheaves of sets.

## References

Stacks Project, tag 0738 (`sites-lemma-directed-colimits-sections`); it is the analogue for sites
of Stacks 009F for topological spaces, and Stacks 0GMR is the variant for global sections on a
quasi-compact topos.
-/

section

universe w₃ w₂ w₁ v u
open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

namespace Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections

@[expose] public section

/-! ### Finite families in a filtered category -/

section Filtered

variable {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I] [IsFiltered I]

/-- In a filtered category, a finite family of morphisms `w t : i₀ ⟶ k t` out of a fixed object
`i₀` can be completed by morphisms `v t : k t ⟶ k'` to a single morphism `w' : i₀ ⟶ k'`, i.e.
so that `w t ≫ v t = w'` for every `t`. -/
private lemma exists_comp_eq_of_finite {T : Type*} [Finite T] (i₀ : I) (k : T → I)
    (w : ∀ t, i₀ ⟶ k t) : ∃ (k' : I) (w' : i₀ ⟶ k') (v : ∀ t, k t ⟶ k'), ∀ t, w t ≫ v t = w' := by
  classical
  have : Fintype T := Fintype.ofFinite T
  let O : Finset I := insert i₀ (Finset.univ.image k)
  have hi₀ : i₀ ∈ O := Finset.mem_insert_self _ _
  have hk : ∀ t, k t ∈ O := fun t =>
    Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image_of_mem k (Finset.mem_univ t))
  let H : Finset (Σ' (X Y : I) (_ : X ∈ O) (_ : Y ∈ O), X ⟶ Y) :=
    Finset.univ.image (fun t : T => ⟨i₀, k t, hi₀, hk t, w t⟩)
  exact
    ⟨IsFiltered.sup O H, IsFiltered.toSup O H hi₀, fun t => IsFiltered.toSup O H (hk t), fun t =>
      IsFiltered.toSup_commutes O H hi₀ (hk t) (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ t))⟩

/-- In a filtered category, a finite family of objects admits a morphism from each of its members
to one object. -/
private lemma exists_hom_of_finite {T : Type*} [Finite T] (k : T → I) :
    ∃ k' : I, ∀ t, Nonempty (k t ⟶ k') := by
  classical
  have : Fintype T := Fintype.ofFinite T
  obtain ⟨k', hk'⟩ := IsFiltered.sup_objs_exists (Finset.univ.image k)
  exact ⟨k', fun t => hk' (Finset.mem_image_of_mem k (Finset.mem_univ t))⟩

end Filtered

/-! ### Generalities on sites -/

section Site

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- A monomorphism of sheaves of types is injective on sections. -/
private lemma injective_app_of_mono {P Q : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {f : P ⟶ Q} (hf : Mono f)
    (V : C) : Function.Injective (f.hom.app (op V)) := by
  have := hf
  exact
    (CategoryTheory.mono_iff_injective _).1 ((NatTrans.mono_iff_mono_app f.hom).1 inferInstance _)

/-- Two sections of a sheaf which agree on a covering sieve are equal. -/
private lemma sheaf_ext {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) {W : C} {S : Sieve W}
    (hS : S ∈ J W) {x y : P.obj (op W)}
    (h : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), S g → P.map g.op x = P.map g.op y) : x = y :=
  (((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J P).1 hP).isSeparated S hS).ext fun _ g hg => h g hg

/-- Two sections of a sheaf which agree after restriction along every member of a covering family
of morphisms with fixed target are equal. -/
private lemma sheaf_ext_of_cover {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) {W : C}
    (𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} W) (h𝒱 : 𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J W) {x y : P.obj (op W)}
    (h : ∀ b, P.map (𝒱.f b).op x = P.map (𝒱.f b).op y) : x = y :=
  𝒱.ext_of_isSeparatedFor
    (Presieve.isSeparatedFor_iff_generate.2
      (((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J P).1 hP).isSeparated _ h𝒱))
    h

/-- A compatible family of sections of a sheaf indexed by a covering family of morphisms with
fixed target glues. -/
private lemma exists_glue {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) {W : C}
    (𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} W) (h𝒱 : 𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J W) (x : ∀ b : 𝒱.I₀, P.obj (op (𝒱.X b)))
    (hx :
      ∀ (b b' : 𝒱.I₀) (Z : C) (p : Z ⟶ 𝒱.X b) (q : Z ⟶ 𝒱.X b'),
        p ≫ 𝒱.f b = q ≫ 𝒱.f b' → P.map p.op (x b) = P.map q.op (x b')) :
    ∃ t : P.obj (op W), ∀ b, P.map (𝒱.f b).op t = x b := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, -⟩ :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff _ _).1
      (((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J P).1 hP).isSheafFor _ h𝒱) x hx
  exact ⟨t, ht⟩

/-- **Two sections of a presheaf which agree after restriction to a pullback of `f` and `g` agree
after restriction along any pair of morphisms with the same composites with `f` and `g`.**

The presheaf takes values in an arbitrary universe, and nothing about the topology is used: this
is pure `CategoryTheory.IsPullback.lift` calculus, and it is the single transfer step of every
diagram chase comparing two sections over a cospan. -/
public lemma map_op_eq_of_comp_eq_of_isPullback {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w₃} {A B X Y : C} {p : X ⟶ A}
    {q : X ⟶ B} {f : A ⟶ Y} {g : B ⟶ Y} (hpb : IsPullback p q f g) {x : P.obj (op A)}
    {y : P.obj (op B)} (h : P.map p.op x = P.map q.op y) {Z : C} (p' : Z ⟶ A) (q' : Z ⟶ B)
    (hpq : p' ≫ f = q' ≫ g) : P.map p'.op x = P.map q'.op y :=
  calc
    P.map p'.op x = P.map (hpb.lift p' q' hpq ≫ p).op x := by rw [hpb.lift_fst]
    _ = P.map (hpb.lift p' q' hpq).op (P.map p.op x) := by rw [op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply]
    _ = P.map (hpb.lift p' q' hpq).op (P.map q.op y) := by rw [h]
    _ = P.map (hpb.lift p' q' hpq ≫ q).op y := by rw [op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply]
    _ = P.map q'.op y := by rw [hpb.lift_snd]

/-- Two sections of a presheaf which agree after restriction to a pullback of `f` and `g` agree
after restriction along any pair of morphisms with the same composites with `f` and `g`. -/
private lemma map_op_eq_of_isPullback {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} {A B X Y : C} {p : X ⟶ A}
    {q : X ⟶ B} {f : A ⟶ Y} {g : B ⟶ Y} (hpb : IsPullback p q f g) {x : P.obj (op A)}
    {y : P.obj (op B)} (h : P.map p.op x = P.map q.op y) {Z : C} (p' : Z ⟶ A) (q' : Z ⟶ B)
    (hpq : p' ≫ f = q' ≫ g) : P.map p'.op x = P.map q'.op y :=
  map_op_eq_of_comp_eq_of_isPullback hpb h p' q' hpq


/-- The family of all the morphisms belonging to a sieve generates that sieve. Its index type lies
in `Type max u v`, so it is an admissible input for
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.IsQuasiCompactObject`. -/
private lemma sieve₀_preZeroHypercover {U : C} (S : Sieve U) :
    S.arrows.preZeroHypercover.sieve₀ = S := by
  rw [PreZeroHypercover.sieve₀, Sieve.ofArrows, ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀,
    Presieve.presieve₀_preZeroHypercover, Sieve.generate_sieve]

/-- Sieve form of **Stacks 090H**: a covering sieve `S` of a quasi-compact object `U` contains a
family `𝒲` of morphisms to `U`, indexed by a finite type, which is refined by a covering family
`𝒱` of `U`. -/
private lemma exists_finite_family_of_isQuasiCompactObject {U : C} (hU : J.IsQuasiCompactObject U)
    {S : Sieve U} (hS : S ∈ J U) :
    ∃ (𝒲 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U) (_ : Finite 𝒲.I₀) (_ : ∀ t, S (𝒲.f t)) (𝒱 :
      PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U) (_ : 𝒱.Hom 𝒲), 𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J U := by
  obtain ⟨𝒱, φ, h𝒱, hfin⟩ :=
    hU S.arrows.preZeroHypercover
      (by rwa [sieve₀_preZeroHypercover])
  exact
    ⟨S.arrows.preZeroHypercover.restrictIndex (fun r : Set.range φ.s₀ => r.1), hfin.to_subtype,
      fun r => r.1.2, 𝒱, { s₀ := fun c => ⟨φ.s₀ c, c, rfl⟩, h₀ := φ.h₀, w₀ := φ.w₀ }, h𝒱⟩

end Site

/-! ### Cofinal systems of finite coverings -/

section FiniteCoverings

/-- Every covering sieve of `U` is refined by a covering family of `U` with finite index type
whose members have pairwise fibre products over `U`, and those fibre products are quasi-compact
objects of the site. This is the hypothesis of part (4) of the source. -/
public def _root_.CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.HasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings
    {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (U : C) : Prop :=
  ∀ S ∈ J U,
    ∃ 𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U,
      Finite 𝒱.I₀ ∧
        𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J U ∧
        𝒱.sieve₀ ≤ S ∧
        ∀ j j' : 𝒱.I₀,
          ∃ (W : C) (p : W ⟶ 𝒱.X j) (q : W ⟶ 𝒱.X j'),
            IsPullback p q (𝒱.f j) (𝒱.f j') ∧ J.IsQuasiCompactObject W

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- An object every covering sieve of which contains the sieve generated by a covering family with
finite index type is quasi-compact: that family refines the given covering, member by member,
through finitely many of its members. -/
private lemma isQuasiCompactObject_of_forall_exists_finite {U : C}
    (H :
      ∀ S ∈ J U,
        ∃ 𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U, Finite 𝒱.I₀ ∧ 𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J U ∧ 𝒱.sieve₀ ≤ S) :
    J.IsQuasiCompactObject U := by
  intro 𝒰 h𝒰
  obtain ⟨𝒱, hfin, h𝒱, hle⟩ := H 𝒰.sieve₀ h𝒰
  choose s α hα using fun c : 𝒱.I₀ => (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).1 (hle _ (𝒱.sieve₀_f c))
  exact ⟨𝒱, ⟨s, α, fun c => (hα c).symm⟩, h𝒱, Set.finite_range _⟩

/-- The hypothesis of part (4) makes `U` quasi-compact; this is how the source invokes
Stacks 0D05. Only the finiteness of the refining families is used, not their fibre products. -/
private lemma isQuasiCompactObject_of_hasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings {U : C}
    (H : J.HasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings U) : J.IsQuasiCompactObject U :=
  isQuasiCompactObject_of_forall_exists_finite fun S hS => by
    obtain ⟨𝒱, hfin, h𝒱, hle, -⟩ := H S hS
    exact ⟨𝒱, hfin, h𝒱, hle⟩

end FiniteCoverings

/-! ### The comparison map -/

section Main

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I]
  [IsFiltered I] [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)] (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v))

/-- Evaluation at `W` takes the colimit of the underlying presheaves to the colimit of the
sections over `W`. -/
private noncomputable def isColimitSections (W : C) :
    IsColimit
      (((evaluation Cᵒᵖ (Type max u v)).obj (op W)).mapCocone
        (colimit.cocone (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)))) :=
  isColimitOfPreserves _ (colimit.isColimit _)

/-- The sheafification of the colimit of the underlying presheaves is the underlying presheaf of
the colimit sheaf: both sheaves are colimits of `F`, by
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.isColimitSheafifyCocone`.

The source is spelled `CategoryTheory.sheafify J _` rather than as the cocone point of
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.sheafifyCocone`, so that the composition of `toSheafify` with this
isomorphism is a composition of two morphisms whose middle object is syntactically the one
occurring in the instances `Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify'` and
`Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_toSheafify'`. -/
private noncomputable def sheafifyIso :
    CategoryTheory.sheafify J (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) ≅ (colimit F).obj :=
  (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)).mapIso
    (IsColimit.coconePointUniqueUpToIso
      (Sheaf.isColimitSheafifyCocone (colimit.cocone (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)))
        (colimit.isColimit _))
      (colimit.isColimit F))

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- The canonical map from the colimit of the underlying presheaves to the underlying presheaf of
the colimit sheaf is the sheafification map, up to the isomorphism of the two colimits. -/
private lemma toSheafify_comp_eq :
    CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) ≫
        (sheafifyIso F).hom =
      colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) := by
  refine colimit.hom_ext fun i => ?_
  have h :
    ((Sheaf.sheafifyCocone (colimit.cocone (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)))).ι.app i).hom =
      colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i ≫
        CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) :=
    Sheaf.sheafifyCocone_ι_app_val _ i
  rw [colimit.ι_post, ← Category.assoc, ← h]
  exact
    congrArg (fun f : F.obj i ⟶ colimit F => f.hom)
      (IsColimit.comp_coconePointUniqueUpToIso_hom _ (colimit.isColimit F) i)

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- A section of the colimit sheaf is locally in the image of the presheaf colimit, because the
comparison map is the sheafification map up to the isomorphism of the two colimits. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_post :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) := by
  rw [← toSheafify_comp_eq F]
  exact
    Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_comp J
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))))
      (sheafifyIso F).hom

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- A section of the colimit sheaf is locally in the image of the presheaf colimit, because the
comparison map is the sheafification map up to the isomorphism of the two colimits. -/
alias isLocallySurjective_post' := isLocallySurjective_post

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Two sections of the presheaf colimit with the same image in the colimit sheaf agree locally,
because the comparison map is the sheafification map up to the isomorphism of the two colimits. -/
private lemma isLocallyInjective_post :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) := by
  rw [← toSheafify_comp_eq F]
  exact
    Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_comp J
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))))
      (sheafifyIso F).hom

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Two sections of the presheaf colimit with the same image in the colimit sheaf agree locally,
because the comparison map is the sheafification map up to the isomorphism of the two colimits. -/
alias isLocallyInjective_post' := isLocallyInjective_post

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- The comparison map, on the presheaf colimit, is described by the components of the colimit
cocone of `F`. -/
private lemma post_app_ι (W : C) (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))).app (op W)
        ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) s) =
      (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) s :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (NatTrans.congr_app (colimit.ι_post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i) (op W)) s

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- `Ψ` is described by the components of the colimit cocone of `F`. -/
private lemma post_sections_ι (W : C) (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W))
        (colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i s) =
      (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) s :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (colimit.ι_post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i) s

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- The components of the colimit cocone of `F` are compatible with the transition maps. -/
private lemma ι_app_map {i k : I} (w : i ⟶ k) (W : C) (x : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op W) ((F.map w).hom.app (op W) x) =
      (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) x := by
  conv_rhs => rw [← colimit.w F w]
  rfl

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- The components of the colimit cocone of the diagram of sections are compatible with the
transition maps. -/
private lemma ι_sections_map {i k : I} (w : i ⟶ k) (W : C) (x : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) k ((F.map w).hom.app (op W) x) =
      colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i x :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (colimit.w (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) w) x

omit [IsFiltered I] [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type (max u v))] in
/-- Naturality of a transition map, on sections. -/
private lemma map_naturality_apply {i k : I} (w : i ⟶ k) {V W : C} (g : V ⟶ W)
    (x : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    (F.map w).hom.app (op V) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op x) =
      (F.obj k).obj.map g.op ((F.map w).hom.app (op W) x) :=
  NatTrans.naturality_apply (F.map w).hom g.op x

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Naturality of a component of the colimit cocone of `F`, on sections. -/
private lemma ι_naturality_apply (k : I) {V W : C} (g : V ⟶ W) (x : (F.obj k).obj.obj (op W)) :
    (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op V) ((F.obj k).obj.map g.op x) =
      (colimit F).obj.map g.op ((colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op W) x) :=
  NatTrans.naturality_apply (colimit.ι F k).hom g.op x

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Naturality of a component of the colimit cocone of the diagram of underlying presheaves. -/
private lemma ι_pre_naturality_apply (i : I) {V W : C} (g : V ⟶ W) (x : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)) :
    (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op V) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op x) =
      (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))).map g.op
        ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) x) :=
  NatTrans.naturality_apply (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i) g.op x

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Every section of the colimit sheaf is locally in the image of some `F i`. -/
private lemma exists_local_section (W : C) (t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op W)) :
    ∃ S : Sieve W,
      S ∈ J W ∧
        ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W),
          S g →
            ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op V)),
              (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op V) s = (colimit F).obj.map g.op t := by
  have := isLocallySurjective_post F
  refine
    ⟨Presheaf.imageSieve (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) t,
      Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) t,
      fun V g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨i, s, hs⟩ := Types.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit (isColimitSections F V) x
  have hs' : (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op V) s = x := hs
  exact
    ⟨i, s, by
      rwa [← post_app_ι F V i s, hs']⟩

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Every section of the colimit sheaf is locally in the image of some `F i`. -/
alias exists_local_section' := exists_local_section

/-- Two sections of `F i` with the same image in the colimit sheaf agree locally after a
transition map. -/
private lemma exists_local_transition (W : C) (i : I) (a b : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W))
    (h : (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) a = (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) b) :
    ∃ S : Sieve W,
      S ∈ J W ∧
        ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W),
          S g →
            ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k),
              (F.map w).hom.app (op V) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op a) =
                (F.map w).hom.app (op V) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op b) := by
  have := isLocallyInjective_post F
  refine
    ⟨Presheaf.equalizerSieve ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) a)
        ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) b),
      Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))) _ _
        (by rwa [post_app_ι, post_app_ι]),
      fun V g hg => ?_⟩
  have key :
    (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op V) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op a) =
      (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op V)
        ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op b) := by
    rwa [ι_pre_naturality_apply, ι_pre_naturality_apply]
  exact (Types.FilteredColimit.isColimit_eq_iff' (isColimitSections F V) _ _).1 key

/-- Two sections of `F i` with the same image in the colimit sheaf agree locally after a
transition map. -/
alias exists_local_transition' := exists_local_transition

/-! ### Injectivity and surjectivity of `Ψ` from the two local statements -/

/-- `Ψ` is injective as soon as two sections of some `F i` over `W` with the same image in the
colimit sheaf agree after a transition map. -/
private lemma injective_post_sections (W : C)
    (hcore :
      ∀ (i : I) (a b : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)),
        (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) a = (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) b →
          ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k), (F.map w).hom.app (op W) a = (F.map w).hom.app (op W) b) :
    Function.Injective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W))) := by
  intro x y hxy
  obtain ⟨i, a, b, ha, hb⟩ :=
    Types.FilteredColimit.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit₂
      (colimit.isColimit (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W))) x y
  have ha' : colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i a = x := ha
  have hb' : colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i b = y := hb
  subst ha'
  subst hb'
  rw [post_sections_ι, post_sections_ι] at hxy
  obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ := hcore i a b hxy
  rw [← ι_sections_map F w W a, ← ι_sections_map F w W b, hw]

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- `Ψ` is surjective as soon as every section of the colimit sheaf over `W` comes from some
`F i`. -/
private lemma surjective_post_sections (W : C)
    (hcore :
      ∀ t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op W),
        ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W)), (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) s = t) :
    Function.Surjective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W))) := by
  intro t
  obtain ⟨i, s, hs⟩ := hcore t
  exact
    ⟨colimit.ι (F ⋙ (sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op W)) i s, by
      rwa [post_sections_ι]⟩

/-! ### Steps common to several of the four parts -/

omit [IsFiltered I] [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type (max u v))] in
/-- The transition step of parts (2) and (4). Let `x` and `y` be sections of `F i` over `Y` and
`Y'`, and let `g : Z ⟶ Y` and `g' : Z ⟶ Y'`. If the restrictions of `x` along `g` and of `y` along
`g'` become equal after the transition map `w₀ : i ⟶ k`, then the images of `x` and `y` under any
transition map `w` factoring through `w₀` already have equal restrictions along `g` and `g'`. -/
private lemma map_op_map_app_eq_of_comp_eq {i k k' : I} {w₀ : i ⟶ k} {v : k ⟶ k'} {w : i ⟶ k'}
    (hw : w₀ ≫ v = w) {Y Y' Z : C} {x : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op Y)} {y : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op Y')}
    (g : Z ⟶ Y) (g' : Z ⟶ Y')
    (h :
      (F.map w₀).hom.app (op Z) ((F.obj i).obj.map g.op x) =
        (F.map w₀).hom.app (op Z) ((F.obj i).obj.map g'.op y)) :
    (F.obj k').obj.map g.op ((F.map w).hom.app (op Y) x) =
      (F.obj k').obj.map g'.op ((F.map w).hom.app (op Y') y) := by
  subst hw
  rw [← map_naturality_apply, ← map_naturality_apply, F.map_comp]
  exact congrArg ((F.map v).hom.app (op Z)) h

/-- Finitely many sections of the colimit sheaf, each of them in the image of some `F i`, are all
in the image of a single `F k`. -/
private lemma exists_sections_common_index {T : Type*} [Finite T] {Y : T → C}
    {t : ∀ b, (colimit F).obj.obj (op (Y b))}
    (h :
      ∀ b,
        ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op (Y b))), (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op (Y b)) s = t b) :
    ∃ (k : I) (σ : ∀ b, (F.obj k).obj.obj (op (Y b))),
      ∀ b, (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op (Y b)) (σ b) = t b := by
  choose i s hs using h
  obtain ⟨k, u⟩ := exists_hom_of_finite i
  exact
    ⟨k, fun b => (F.map (u b).some).hom.app (op (Y b)) (s b), fun b => by
      rw [ι_app_map]; exact hs b⟩

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- Two sections of `F k`, over objects `A` and `B` of `C`, whose images in the colimit sheaf are
restrictions of one section `t` over `U`, have the same image in the colimit sheaf after
restriction along any pair of morphisms into `A` and `B` with equal composites to `U`. -/
private lemma ι_app_map_op_eq (k : I) {U A B Z : C} {t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op U)}
    {x : (F.obj k).obj.obj (op A)} {y : (F.obj k).obj.obj (op B)} {f : A ⟶ U} {g : B ⟶ U}
    (hx : (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op A) x = (colimit F).obj.map f.op t)
    (hy : (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op B) y = (colimit F).obj.map g.op t) (p : Z ⟶ A) (q : Z ⟶ B)
    (hpq : p ≫ f = q ≫ g) :
    (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op Z) ((F.obj k).obj.map p.op x) =
      (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op Z) ((F.obj k).obj.map q.op y) := by
  rw [ι_naturality_apply, ι_naturality_apply, hx, hy, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ←
    Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, ← op_comp, hpq]

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- If a covering family `𝒱` of `U` carries a compatible family of sections of a single `F k`
whose images in the colimit sheaf are the restrictions of `t`, then `t` is the image of a section
of `F k` over `U`. -/
private lemma exists_section_of_glue {U : C} (t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op U))
    (𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U) (h𝒱 : 𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J U) (k : I)
    (τ : ∀ c, (F.obj k).obj.obj (op (𝒱.X c)))
    (hτ : ∀ c, (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op (𝒱.X c)) (τ c) = (colimit F).obj.map (𝒱.f c).op t)
    (hcompat :
      ∀ (c c' : 𝒱.I₀) (Z : C) (p : Z ⟶ 𝒱.X c) (q : Z ⟶ 𝒱.X c'),
        p ≫ 𝒱.f c = q ≫ 𝒱.f c' → (F.obj k).obj.map p.op (τ c) = (F.obj k).obj.map q.op (τ c')) :
    ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op U)), (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op U) s = t := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_glue (F.obj k).property 𝒱 h𝒱 τ hcompat
  exact
    ⟨k, s,
      sheaf_ext_of_cover (colimit F).property 𝒱 h𝒱 fun c => by rw [← ι_naturality_apply, hs, hτ]⟩

/-! ### Part (1): injective transition maps -/

/-- If all the transition maps are injective on sections, then so is each component of the colimit
cocone of the diagram of underlying presheaves. -/
private lemma injective_ι_pre_app (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) (V : C)
    (i : I) :
    Function.Injective ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op V)) := by
  intro a b h
  obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ := (Types.FilteredColimit.isColimit_eq_iff' (isColimitSections F V) a b).1 h
  exact injective_app_of_mono (hmono _ _ w) V hw

/-- If all the transition maps are injective then the colimit of the underlying presheaves is
separated: this is the presheaf `F'` of the source's proof of part (1). -/
private lemma separated_colimit_presheaf (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) {W : C}
    {S : Sieve W} (hS : S ∈ J W)
    {x y : (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))).obj (op W)}
    (h :
      ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W),
        S g →
          (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))).map g.op x =
            (colimit (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v))).map g.op y) :
    x = y := by
  obtain ⟨i, a, b, ha, hb⟩ :=
    Types.FilteredColimit.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit₂ (isColimitSections F W) x y
  have ha' : (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) a = x := ha
  have hb' : (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) b = y := hb
  subst ha'
  subst hb'
  refine
    congrArg (fun z => (colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) z)
      (sheaf_ext (F.obj i).property hS fun V g hg => ?_)
  refine injective_ι_pre_app F hmono V i ?_
  rw [ι_pre_naturality_apply, ι_pre_naturality_apply]
  exact h g hg

/-- **Part (1)** of the source, in the form used by the rest of the argument. -/
private lemma exists_transition_of_mono (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) (W : C)
    (i : I) (a b : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W))
    (h : (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) a = (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) b) :
    ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k), (F.map w).hom.app (op W) a = (F.map w).hom.app (op W) b := by
  have := isLocallyInjective_post F
  refine
    (Types.FilteredColimit.isColimit_eq_iff' (isColimitSections F W) a b).1
      (separated_colimit_presheaf F hmono
        (Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J (colimit.post F (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)))
          ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) a)
          ((colimit.ι (F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)) i).app (op W) b)
          (by rwa [post_app_ι, post_app_ι]))
        ?_)
  exact fun _ _ hg => hg

/-- **Part (1)** of the source, in the form used in part (3): if all the transition maps are
injective on sections then so is each component of the colimit cocone of `F`. -/
private lemma injective_ι_app_of_mono (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) (W : C)
    (i : I) : Function.Injective ((colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W)) := by
  intro a b h
  obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ := exists_transition_of_mono F hmono W i a b h
  exact injective_app_of_mono (hmono _ _ w) W hw

/-! ### Part (2): quasi-compact objects -/

/-- **Part (2)** of the source, in the form used by the rest of the argument. -/
private lemma exists_transition_of_isQuasiCompactObject {W : C} (hW : J.IsQuasiCompactObject W)
    (i : I) (a b : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op W))
    (h : (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) a = (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op W) b) :
    ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k), (F.map w).hom.app (op W) a = (F.map w).hom.app (op W) b := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hSloc⟩ := exists_local_transition F W i a b h
  obtain ⟨𝒲, hfin, hS𝒲, 𝒱, φ, h𝒱⟩ := exists_finite_family_of_isQuasiCompactObject hW hS
  choose k₁ w₁ hw₁ using fun t : 𝒲.I₀ => hSloc (𝒲.f t) (hS𝒲 t)
  obtain ⟨k, w, v, hv⟩ := exists_comp_eq_of_finite i k₁ w₁
  refine ⟨k, w, sheaf_ext_of_cover (F.obj k).property 𝒱 h𝒱 fun c => ?_⟩
  rw [← φ.w₀ c, op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply, Functor.map_comp_apply,
    map_op_map_app_eq_of_comp_eq F (hv (φ.s₀ c)) (𝒲.f (φ.s₀ c)) (𝒲.f (φ.s₀ c)) (hw₁ (φ.s₀ c))]

/-! ### Part (3): surjectivity for a quasi-compact object with injective transition maps -/

/-- **Part (3)** of the source, in the form from which surjectivity of `Ψ` is read off: the local
sections provided by quasi-compactness live over a single index, and glue there. -/
private lemma exists_section_of_isQuasiCompactObject_of_mono
    (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) {U : C} (hU : J.IsQuasiCompactObject U)
    (t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op U)), (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op U) s = t := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hSloc⟩ := exists_local_section F U t
  obtain ⟨𝒲, hfin, hS𝒲, 𝒱, φ, h𝒱⟩ := exists_finite_family_of_isQuasiCompactObject hU hS
  obtain ⟨k, σ, hσ⟩ := exists_sections_common_index F fun b : 𝒲.I₀ => hSloc (𝒲.f b) (hS𝒲 b)
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ :
    ∃ τ : ∀ c : 𝒱.I₀, (F.obj k).obj.obj (op (𝒱.X c)),
      ∀ c, (colimit.ι F k).hom.app (op (𝒱.X c)) (τ c) = (colimit F).obj.map (𝒱.f c).op t :=
    ⟨fun c => (F.obj k).obj.map (φ.h₀ c).op (σ (φ.s₀ c)), fun c => by
      rw [ι_naturality_apply, hσ, ← φ.w₀ c, op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply]⟩
  exact
    exists_section_of_glue F t 𝒱 h𝒱 k τ hτ fun c c' Z p q hpq =>
      injective_ι_app_of_mono F hmono Z k (ι_app_map_op_eq F k (hτ c) (hτ c') p q hpq)

/-! ### Part (4): surjectivity for a cofinal system of finite coverings -/

/-- **Part (4)** of the source, in the form from which surjectivity of `Ψ` is read off: here the
covering family is finite from the outset, and compatibility of the resulting sections comes from
part (2) applied to the pairwise pullbacks. -/
private lemma exists_section_of_hasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings {U : C}
    (H : J.HasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings U) (t : (colimit F).obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (i : I) (s : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op U)), (colimit.ι F i).hom.app (op U) s = t := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hSloc⟩ := exists_local_section F U t
  obtain ⟨𝒱, hfin, h𝒱, hle, hsq⟩ := H S hS
  obtain ⟨k, σ, hσ⟩ :=
    exists_sections_common_index F fun c : 𝒱.I₀ => hSloc (𝒱.f c) (hle _ (𝒱.sieve₀_f c))
  choose W p q hpb hWqc using fun z : 𝒱.I₀ × 𝒱.I₀ => hsq z.1 z.2
  choose k₁ w₁ hw₁ using fun z : 𝒱.I₀ × 𝒱.I₀ =>
    exists_transition_of_isQuasiCompactObject F (hWqc z) k ((F.obj k).obj.map (p z).op (σ z.1))
      ((F.obj k).obj.map (q z).op (σ z.2))
      (ι_app_map_op_eq F k (hσ z.1) (hσ z.2) (p z) (q z) (hpb z).w)
  obtain ⟨k', w, v, hv⟩ := exists_comp_eq_of_finite k k₁ w₁
  exact
    exists_section_of_glue F t 𝒱 h𝒱 k' (fun c => (F.map w).hom.app (op (𝒱.X c)) (σ c))
      (fun c => by
        rw [ι_app_map]; exact hσ c)
      fun c c' Z p' q' hpq' =>
      map_op_eq_of_comp_eq_of_isPullback (hpb (c, c'))
        (map_op_map_app_eq_of_comp_eq F (hv (c, c')) (p (c, c')) (q (c, c')) (hw₁ (c, c'))) p' q'
        hpq'

end Main

end

end Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections

namespace CategoryTheory.Sheaf

@[expose] public section

open Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections in
/-- **Stacks 0738.** Let `C` be a site, `F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)` a filtered diagram of
sheaves of sets and `U` an object of `C`. For the canonical map
`Ψ = colimit.post F ((sheafSections J _).obj (op U)) : colim_i F_i(U) ⟶ (colim_i F_i)(U)`:

1. if every transition map `F.map f` is a monomorphism, then `Ψ` is injective;
2. if `U` is quasi-compact (Stacks 090H), then `Ψ` is injective;
3. if `U` is quasi-compact and every transition map is a monomorphism, then `Ψ` is bijective;
4. if the coverings `{U_j ⟶ U}_{j ∈ J}` with `J` finite and all fibre products `U_j ×_U U_{j'}`
   existing and quasi-compact are cofinal among the coverings of `U`, then `Ψ` is bijective.

The four conjuncts are the four parts of the source, in order. -/
@[stacks 0738 "Sections over U of a filtered colimit of sheaves of sets.",
  sga "4 VI 1.23" "(i) qc ⇒ inj"]
public theorem injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_sheafSections {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I] [IsFiltered I]
    [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)] (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)) (U : C) :
    ((∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Injective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op U)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactObject U →
        Function.Injective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op U)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactObject U →
        (∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op U)))) ∧
      ((∀ S ∈ J U,
          ∃ 𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U,
            Finite 𝒱.I₀ ∧
              𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ J U ∧
              𝒱.sieve₀ ≤ S ∧
              ∀ j j' : 𝒱.I₀,
                ∃ (W : C) (p : W ⟶ 𝒱.X j) (q : W ⟶ 𝒱.X j'),
                  IsPullback p q (𝒱.f j) (𝒱.f j') ∧ J.IsQuasiCompactObject W) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F ((sheafSections J (Type max u v)).obj (op U)))) :=
  ⟨fun hmono => injective_post_sections F U (exists_transition_of_mono F hmono U), fun hU =>
    injective_post_sections F U (exists_transition_of_isQuasiCompactObject F hU), fun hU hmono =>
    ⟨injective_post_sections F U (exists_transition_of_mono F hmono U),
      surjective_post_sections F U (exists_section_of_isQuasiCompactObject_of_mono F hmono hU)⟩,
    fun H =>
    ⟨injective_post_sections F U
        (exists_transition_of_isQuasiCompactObject F
          (isQuasiCompactObject_of_hasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings H)),
      surjective_post_sections F U (exists_section_of_hasFiniteQuasiCompactCoverings F H)⟩⟩

end

end CategoryTheory.Sheaf

end

/-!
# The topos-theoretic meaning of a quasi-compact object of a site

Let `C` be a site and `U` an object of `C`. There are two notions of quasi-compactness in play,
one for each of the two categories:

* in the *site*, `U` is quasi-compact when every covering of `U` is refined by a covering that
  factors through only finitely many of its members (Stacks 090H);
* in the *topos* `Sh(C)` of sheaves of sets, an object is quasi-compact when every surjection
  onto it from a coproduct `∐_{i ∈ I} F i` already admits a surjection from the coproduct over
  some finite `T ⊆ I` (Stacks 0D07).

The two agree along the Yoneda embedding: `U` is a quasi-compact object of the site exactly when
the sheafified representable `h_U^#` is a quasi-compact object of the topos. So the second
notion, which never mentions the coverings of `U` directly, is the intrinsic meaning of the
first.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isQuasiCompactObject_iff_isQuasiCompact_sheafifiedYoneda`:
  the equivalence of Stacks 0D06.
* `Stacks.Sites.QuasiCompactCriterion.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_sheafifiedYoneda_map_iff`:
  **Stacks 00WT** for
  sheafified representables — a family of morphisms generates a covering sieve exactly when the
  morphism it induces out of the coproduct of their sheafified representables is a surjection.
  Used in the proof below and by Stacks 0GMS case (2).

## Implementation notes

All three notions the statement needs already have names here, so the lemma is an equivalence
between two named predicates rather than a restatement of either. Condition (2) of the source is
literally `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact` (Stacks 0D07), including its reading of
"surjection of sheaves" as local surjectivity (Stacks 00WM (2), Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective`) and its coproducts taken in `Sheaf J (Type max u v)`
— i.e. the sheafification of the coproduct of presheaves, which is the coproduct the source's own
proof analyses (Stacks 00WI). Condition (1) is
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.IsQuasiCompactObject` (Stacks 090H). The sheaf `h_U^#` is
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J`, the sheafified Yoneda embedding already used for
Stacks 0GLW, evaluated at `U`.

Departures from the wording of the source, none of them weakenings:

* The topos of sheaves of sets on a category `C : Type u` with `Category.{v} C` is taken in
  `Type max u v`, where sheafification exists unconditionally
  (`CategoryTheory.instHasSheafifyType`), whereas `yoneda.obj U` lands in `Type v`. Accordingly
  `sheafifiedYoneda` sheafifies `CategoryTheory.uliftYoneda`, Mathlib's representable presheaf
  valued in the larger universe. This is the source's `h_U` followed by a universe lift and not a
  different presheaf: for a site in the sense of the source, whose underlying category is small,
  `v = u` and `CategoryTheory.uliftYonedaIsoYoneda` identifies the two.
* The statement is for an arbitrary `Category.{v} C` rather than only a small one, which is the
  shape all three cited declarations already have.
* "there is a finite subset `J ⊆ I`" is `∃ T : Set I, T.Finite`, and the index type `I` ranges
  over `Type max u v`, which is the size of index type the coproducts of the topos accept; the
  source leaves `I` unrestricted.

Faithfulness:

1. Every hypothesis is used: the only data are the site `J` and the object `U`, and both sides of
   the equivalence mention both. Being an `Iff`, neither side is decoration on the other.
2. The base is the source's: the site is the given `C` with the given topology `J`, and the topos
   is sheaves of *sets* on it, with coproducts and surjectivity computed in
   `Sheaf J (Type max u v)` rather than in presheaves.
3. The canonical map is pinned: `h_U^#` is the sheafification of the representable at `U`, not
   some sheaf isomorphic to it, and the surjection `∐_{i ∈ T} F i ⟶ h_U^#` of (2) is pinned as the
   map `CategoryTheory.Limits.Sigma.desc` induced by the given family restricted to `T`, not
   merely asserted to exist.
4. Not degenerate: for the trivial topology `⊥` every object of the site is quasi-compact
   (`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isQuasiCompactObject_bot`), so both sides have content
   there; and no hypothesis restricts `C`, `J` or `U` beyond being a site and an object of it.

## References

Stacks Project, tag 0D06 (`sites-lemma-quasi-compact`), the lemma giving the topos-theoretic
meaning of quasi-compactness of an object; its two notions are tags 090H and 0D07, and its proof
uses tags 00WI and 00WT. Quasi-compactness transfers along locally surjective maps by tag 0GMP.
-/

section

universe v u
open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite
variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

namespace Stacks.Sites.QuasiCompactCriterion

section Fac

variable {F₁ F₂ F₃ : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {f₁ : F₁ ⟶ F₂} {f₂ : F₂ ⟶ F₃} {f₃ : F₁ ⟶ F₃}

/-- Sheaf-level form of `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac`: precomposing with
a surjection of sheaves does not change surjectivity. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac (fac : f₁ ≫ f₂ = f₃) [Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₁] :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₃ ↔ Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₂ := by
  refine Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac J (f₁ := f₁.hom) (f₃ := f₃.hom) ?_
  rw [← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, fac]

end Fac

/-! ### Stacks 00WT for sheaves of sets -/

/-- **Stacks 00WT.** A family of morphisms `{X i ⟶ S}` generates a covering sieve of `S` if and
only if the induced morphism `∐_i h_{X i}^# ⟶ h_S^#` is a surjection of sheaves, i.e. is locally
surjective.

This is `public` rather than `private` because it is the only form of Stacks 00WT in either tree
for sheafified representables at index universe `Type max u v`, in both directions; the public
`stacks_00WT` of `StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Representable.CoproductYonedaDesc` is the
presheaf-level forward implication for an index in `Type v`. Stacks 0GMS case (2) consumes it. -/
public lemma isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_sheafifiedYoneda_map_iff {S : C} {ι : Type max u v}
    {X : ι → C} (p : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S) :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i)) ↔
      Sieve.ofArrows X p ∈ J S := by
  -- sheafification commutes with the coproduct, its comparison morphism being an isomorphism —
  -- hence a surjection — because `presheafToSheaf` is a left adjoint
  have fac :
    (sigmaComparison (presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)) fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (X i)) ≫
        (presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).map
          (Limits.Sigma.desc fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.map (p i)) =
      Limits.Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i) :=
    sigmaComparison_map_desc _ _ _ _
  exact
    (isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac fac).trans
      ((Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_presheafToSheaf_map_iff J
            (Limits.Sigma.desc fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.map (p i))).trans
        (J.ofArrows_mem_iff_isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_uliftYoneda_map p).symm)

/-! ### Stacks 00WI: a section of a coproduct of sheaves is locally a section of one summand -/

section JointRange

variable {I : Type max u v} {G : I → Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {F : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}

/-- A section of `F` lies in the join of the images of a family `f i : G i ⟶ F` exactly when it
lies in the image of a single `f i`. -/
private lemma mem_iSup_range_iff (f : ∀ i, G i ⟶ F) (Y : Cᵒᵖ) (x : F.obj.obj Y) :
    x ∈ (⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (f i).hom).obj Y ↔
      ∃ (i : I) (t : (G i).obj.obj Y), (f i).hom.app Y t = x := by
  simp

/-- **Stacks 00WI**, in the form the proof of Stacks 0D06 uses: if the morphism
`∐_{i ∈ I} G i ⟶ F` induced by a family of morphisms of sheaves of sets is a surjection, then every
section of `F` lies, locally, in the image of a single member of the family. -/
private lemma sieveOfSection_iSup_range_mem {f : ∀ i, G i ⟶ F}
    (hf : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc f)) {Y : Cᵒᵖ} (s : F.obj.obj Y) :
    (⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (f i).hom).sieveOfSection s ∈ J Y.unop := by
  have hs : s ∈ ((⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (f i).hom).sheafify J).obj Y := by
    rw [CategoryTheory.Sheaf.sheafify_eq_top_of_range_le hf (⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (f i).hom)
        (le_iSup fun i ↦ Subfunctor.range (f i).hom)]
    simp
  unfold Subfunctor.sheafify at hs
  exact hs

end JointRange

/-! ### Morphisms over `U` out of a sheafified representable -/

/-- **The parenthetical remark of the source's proof.** Let `p : F ⟶ h_U^#` and let `t` be a
section of `F` over `V` whose image under `p` is the restriction of the tautological section along
`g : V ⟶ U` — the source's "`s_a` maps to `id_U|_{U_a}`". Then `t` is a morphism over `U`: for
every `h : W ⟶ V`, the morphism `h_W^# ⟶ F` corresponding to `t|_W` composes with `p` to the
morphism `h_{h ≫ g}^#` induced by `h ≫ g : W ⟶ U`. -/
private lemma comp_eq_sheafifiedYoneda_map {F : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {W V U : C}
    {p : F ⟶ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U} {g : V ⟶ U} {t : F.obj.obj (op V)}
    (ht :
      p.hom.app (op V) t =
        ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U).obj.map g.op (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J U))
    (h : W ⟶ V) :
    (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).symm (F.obj.map h.op t) ≫ p =
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (h ≫ g) := by
  apply (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).injective
  rw [Sheaf.sectionEquiv_comp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, NatTrans.naturality_apply, ht, ←
    Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, Sheaf.map_op_tautologicalSection]

end Stacks.Sites.QuasiCompactCriterion

namespace CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology

@[expose] public section

open Stacks.Sites.QuasiCompactCriterion in
/-- **Stacks 0D06.** Let `C` be a site and `U` an object of `C`. The following are equivalent:

1. `U` is a quasi-compact object of the site (Stacks 090H): every covering of `U` is refined by a
   covering that factors through only finitely many of its members;
2. for every surjection of sheaves `∐_{i ∈ I} F i ⟶ h_U^#` there is a finite `T ⊆ I` for which
   `∐_{i ∈ T} F i ⟶ h_U^#` is still surjective, i.e. `h_U^#` is a quasi-compact object of the
   topos `Sh(C)` (Stacks 0D07).

Here `h_U^# = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U` is the sheafification of the presheaf represented
by `U`. -/
@[stacks 0D06 "An object of a site is quasi-compact if and only if the sheafification of the
  presheaf it represents is a quasi-compact object of the topos of sheaves of sets.", sga
    "4 VI 1.2"]
public theorem isQuasiCompactObject_iff_isQuasiCompact_sheafifiedYoneda {C : Type u}
    [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (U : C) :
    J.IsQuasiCompactObject U ↔ Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U) := by
  constructor
  · -- (1) ⇒ (2)
    intro hU I G f hf
    -- `id_U` lies locally in the image of a single `G i` (Stacks 00WI), so there is a covering
    -- `{V a ⟶ U}` and for each `a` a section of `G (idx a)` over `V a` mapping to `id_U|_{V a}`
    obtain ⟨A, V, r, hVr⟩ :=
      Sieve.exists_eq_ofArrows
        ((⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (f i).hom).sieveOfSection (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J U))
    have hcov : Sieve.ofArrows V r ∈ J U :=
      hVr ▸ sieveOfSection_iSup_range_mem hf (Y := op U) (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J U)
    have hsec :
      ∀ a : A,
        ∃ (i : I) (t : (G i).obj.obj (op (V a))),
          (f i).hom.app (op (V a)) t =
            ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U).obj.map (r a).op
              (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J U) := by
      intro a
      rw [← mem_iSup_range_iff]
      have ha : Sieve.ofArrows V r (r a) := Sieve.ofArrows_mk V r a
      rw [← hVr] at ha
      exact ha
    choose idx t ht using hsec
    -- quasi-compactness of `U` refines `{V a ⟶ U}` to a covering hitting finitely many `a`
    obtain ⟨𝒱, φ, h𝒱, hfin⟩ := hU { I₀ := A, X := V, f := r } hcov
    -- each member of the refined covering is a morphism over `U` into one `G (idx (φ.s₀ b))`
    have hm :
      ∀ b : 𝒱.I₀,
        ∃ m : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (𝒱.X b) ⟶ G (idx (φ.s₀ b)),
          m ≫ f (idx (φ.s₀ b)) = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (𝒱.f b) :=
      fun b ↦
      ⟨(Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).symm ((G (idx (φ.s₀ b))).obj.map (φ.h₀ b).op (t (φ.s₀ b))), by
        rw [comp_eq_sheafifiedYoneda_map (ht (φ.s₀ b)) (φ.h₀ b), φ.w₀ b]⟩
    choose m hm using hm
    -- so the surjection from the refined covering (Stacks 00WT) factors through finitely many `G
    -- i`
    refine
      ⟨Set.range (idx ∘ φ.s₀), by
        rw [Set.range_comp]; exact hfin.image _, ?_⟩
    exact
      CategoryTheory.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_sigmaDesc_fac
        ((isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_sheafifiedYoneda_map_iff 𝒱.f).2 h𝒱)
        (fun b ↦
          m b ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι (fun j : Set.range (idx ∘ φ.s₀) ↦ G (j : I)) ⟨idx (φ.s₀ b), b, rfl⟩)
        (fun b ↦ by
          rw [Category.assoc, Sigma.ι_comp_desc]; exact hm b)
  · -- (2) ⇒ (1)
    intro h2 𝒰 h𝒰
    obtain ⟨T, hTfin, hTls⟩ :=
      h2 𝒰.I₀ (fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (𝒰.X i))
        (fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (𝒰.f i))
        ((isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_sheafifiedYoneda_map_iff 𝒰.f).2 h𝒰)
    refine
      ⟨{ I₀ := T, X := fun j ↦ 𝒰.X j.1, f := fun j ↦ 𝒰.f j.1 },
        { s₀ := fun j ↦ j.1, h₀ := fun _ ↦ 𝟙 _, w₀ := fun _ ↦ Category.id_comp _ },
        (isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_sheafifiedYoneda_map_iff fun j : T ↦ 𝒰.f j.1).1 hTls, ?_⟩
    simpa using hTfin

end

end CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology

end

/-!
# Global sections of a filtered colimit of sheaves of sets

Let `C` be a site and let `F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)`, `i ↦ F i`, be a filtered diagram of
sheaves of sets. Global sections do not in general commute with the colimit: a colimit of sheaves
is the sheafification of the colimit of the underlying presheaves, so the canonical map
`Ψ : colim_i Γ(C, F i) ⟶ Γ(C, colim_i F i)`
need be neither injective nor surjective. It is injective as soon as the transition maps of the
diagram are injective, and also as soon as the topos `Sh(C)` is quasi-compact (Stacks 0D07); it is
bijective when both hold, and also whenever `Sh(C)` admits a set of "covering" objects whose
self-products are quasi-compact.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_globalSections`: the four parts of
  Stacks 0GMR, in order, as the four conjuncts of one statement:
  (1) `Ψ` is injective when every transition map is a monomorphism;
  (2) `Ψ` is injective when the topos `Sh(C)` is quasi-compact;
  (3) `Ψ` is bijective when both hold;
  (4) `Ψ` is bijective when there is a set `S` of sheaves such that every sheaf surjecting onto
  the final sheaf receives a map from a member of `S` which itself surjects onto the final sheaf,
  and such that `K ⨯ K` is quasi-compact for every `K ∈ S`.
* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_prod_snd`: the base change of a surjection onto the
  final sheaf, namely that `prod.snd : G ⨯ K ⟶ K` is locally surjective whenever `G ⟶ *` is.
  This is a step of the proof of part (4), stated separately because it is what verifies
  hypothesis (4)(a) in practice (Stacks 0GMS, Stacks 0GN3).

## Implementation notes

Global sections are `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)`, Mathlib's global sections functor,
the right adjoint of `constantSheaf`; it exists for every site because `Type max u v` has limits
of shape `Cᵒᵖ` (`CategoryTheory.hasGlobalSectionsFunctor_of_hasLimitsOfShape`), so no hypothesis
on `C` is needed. The name spells that functor `globalSections`, which is what Mathlib's own
documentation calls `Γ`, so that the name is readable and the sibling
`injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_sheafSections` (Stacks 0738, sections over an object of the
site) differs from it only in the functor it names. The source instead *defines*
`Γ(C, ℱ) = Mor_{Sh(C)}(*, ℱ)`; the two agree by
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.ΓNatIsoCoyoneda`, which identifies `Γ J (Type max u v)` with the covariant
hom functor of the final sheaf, and injectivity and bijectivity are invariant under that natural
isomorphism. The canonical map is `CategoryTheory.Limits.colimit.post F (Γ J _)`, the map out of
`colim_i Γ(C, F i)` induced by the images under `Γ` of the components of the colimit cocone of
`F`: this is exactly the map `Ψ` of the source, and nothing else pins it, so the statement is
about that map rather than about the existence of some comparison map.

The colimit is formed in `Sheaf J (Type max u v)`, not in presheaves; it exists for every diagram
because sheafification of `Type max u v`-valued presheaves does, so the only smallness hypothesis
is `HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)`, which is what makes the source of `Ψ` exist.
Filteredness of `I` is used by every part: parts (2)-(4) choose an index dominating a finite set
of indices, and part (1) needs `V ↦ colim_i F_i(V)` to be a presheaf whose colimit is filtered in
order for injective transition maps to make it separated.

Points where the form departs from the wording of the source, none of them weakenings:

* "the transition maps are injective" is `Mono (F.map f)` for every morphism `f` of the index
  category. For sheaves of sets this is injectivity on sections over every object of `C`
  (`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.Hom.mono_iff_presheaf_mono` and
  `CategoryTheory.NatTrans.mono_iff_mono_app`); `Mono` is the spelling that does not mention a
  choice of test object.
* "`Ψ` is an isomorphism" (part (3)) and "`Ψ` is bijective" (part (4)) are both
  `Function.Bijective`: in `Type max u v` the isomorphisms are the bijections.
* A surjection of sheaves is a map which is locally surjective (Stacks 00WM (2)), i.e.
  `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective`, and the unique map `𝒦 → *` to the final sheaf is
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.terminal.from`. This is the notion of surjectivity in the definition of
  a quasi-compact object, so (4)(a) and (4)(b) speak of the same thing as (2) and (3) do.
* Quasi-compactness of an object of the topos of sheaves of sets is `Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact` and
  quasi-compactness of the topos itself is `GrothendieckTopology.IsQuasiCompactTopos` (both
  Stacks 0D07). Mathlib's `QuasiCompact` predicates concern schemes and are unrelated.
* `S ⊂ Ob(Sh(C))` is a `Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v))`; the requirement that it be a set rather
  than a class is automatic, the objects of the topos already forming a type. In (4)(a) the map
  `𝒦 → ℱ` is `Nonempty (K ⟶ G)`, because the property required of `𝒦` — that `𝒦 → *` be
  surjective — does not refer to that map. The sheaf called `ℱ` in (4)(a) is called `G` here, the
  letter `F` being taken by the diagram.

Faithfulness:

1. Every hypothesis is used: the four conjuncts carry exactly the premises of the corresponding
   parts of the source and have pairwise different premises, so no part is a decorated special
   case of another; the ambient hypotheses (`IsFiltered I`, the diagram `F`) are the source's
setup. 2. The base is the source's: sheaves of sets on the given site `C` with its given topology
   `J`, with the colimit taken in `Sheaf J (Type max u v)` and not in presheaves.
3. The canonical map is pinned as `colimit.post F (Γ J _)`, not merely asserted to exist.
4. Not degenerate: for the trivial topology `⊥` on a site with a terminal object every presheaf
   is a sheaf and global sections are evaluation at the terminal object
   (`Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections`), so `Ψ` is there the comparison map of a filtered colimit of
   presheaves of sets evaluated at a point, and parts (1) and (3) apply to any such diagram with
   injective transition maps.

## References

Stacks Project, tag 0GMR (`sites-lemma-directed-colimits-global-sections`). Tag 0738 is the
companion statement for sections over an object of the site, and Stacks 0GMS lists concrete
situations in which the hypothesis of part (4) is satisfied.
-/

section

universe w₂ w₁ v u
open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

namespace Stacks.Sites.ColimitGlobalSections

@[expose] public section

/-! ### Finitely many morphisms out of an object of a filtered category -/

section Filtered

variable {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I] [IsFiltered I]

/-- Alias of `Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.exists_comp_eq_of_finite`. -/
private alias exists_comp_eq_of_finite :=
  Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.exists_comp_eq_of_finite

end Filtered

/-! ### Generalities on sheaves of sets -/

section Sheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- Two morphisms of sheaves of sets which take the same value on every section are equal. -/
private lemma hom_ext_sections {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {φ ψ : X ⟶ Y}
    (h : ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), φ.hom.app W x = ψ.hom.app W x) : φ = ψ :=
  Sheaf.hom_ext (NatTrans.ext (funext fun W => ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ (h W)))

/-- Equal morphisms of sheaves of sets take the same value on every section. -/
private lemma congr_app_apply {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {φ ψ : X ⟶ Y} (h : φ = ψ) (W : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : X.obj.obj W) : φ.hom.app W x = ψ.hom.app W x :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (NatTrans.congr_app (congrArg (fun f : X ⟶ Y => f.hom) h) W) x

/-- A composition of morphisms of sheaves of sets acts on sections by composition. -/
private lemma comp_app_apply {X Y Z : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (φ : X ⟶ Y) (ψ : Y ⟶ Z) (W : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : X.obj.obj W) : (φ ≫ ψ).hom.app W x = ψ.hom.app W (φ.hom.app W x) :=
  rfl

/-- A morphism of sheaves of sets commutes with a twofold restriction. -/
private lemma naturality_apply₂ {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (p : X ⟶ Y) {U V W : C} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (g : V ⟶ W) (x : X.obj.obj (op W)) :
    p.hom.app (op U) (X.obj.map h.op (X.obj.map g.op x)) =
      Y.obj.map h.op (Y.obj.map g.op (p.hom.app (op W) x)) := by
  rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply p.hom h.op (X.obj.map g.op x),
    NatTrans.naturality_apply p.hom g.op x]

/-- Alias of `Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.sheaf_ext`. -/
private alias sheaf_ext := Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.sheaf_ext

/-- A compatible family of sections of a sheaf of sets indexed by a covering sieve glues. -/
private lemma exists_glue {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf J P) {W : C}
    {S : Sieve W} (hS : S ∈ J W) (x : Presieve.FamilyOfElements P S.arrows) (hx : x.Compatible) :
    ∃ t : P.obj (op W), ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W) (hg : S g), P.map g.op t = x g hg :=
  ⟨(hP.isSheafFor S hS).amalgamate x hx, fun _ g hg => (hP.isSheafFor S hS).valid_glue hx g hg⟩

/-- A local preimage restricted further is a preimage of the corresponding restriction. -/
private lemma app_map_localPreimage {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ : P ⟶ Q) {W V Z : C}
    (y : Q.obj (op W)) (f : V ⟶ W) (hf : Presheaf.imageSieve φ y f) (k : Z ⟶ V) :
    φ.app (op Z) (P.map k.op (Presheaf.localPreimage φ y f hf)) = Q.map (k ≫ f).op y := by
  rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply φ k.op (Presheaf.localPreimage φ y f hf),
    Presheaf.app_localPreimage]
  exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (Q.map_comp f.op k.op) y).symm

/-- A morphism of sheaves of sets which is injective on the sections over every object of the site
is surjective at every section at which it is locally surjective: the local preimages are then
unique, hence form a compatible family, hence glue. -/
private lemma exists_preimage_of_injective {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (φ : X ⟶ Y)
    (hinj : ∀ V : C, Function.Injective (φ.hom.app (op V))) {W : C} (y : Y.obj.obj (op W))
    (hy : Presheaf.imageSieve φ.hom y ∈ J W) : ∃ x : X.obj.obj (op W), φ.hom.app (op W) x = y := by
  have hglue :=
    exists_glue X.property hy (fun _ g hg => Presheaf.localPreimage φ.hom y g hg)
      (by
        intro _ _ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm
        exact hinj Z (by rw [app_map_localPreimage, app_map_localPreimage, hcomm]))
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hglue
  refine ⟨t, sheaf_ext Y.property hy fun V g hg => ?_⟩
  rw [← NatTrans.naturality_apply φ.hom g.op t, ht g hg, Presheaf.app_localPreimage]

/-- Local surjectivity at a section may be checked locally. -/
lemma imageSieve_mem_of_local {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ : P ⟶ Q) {W : C}
    (y : Q.obj (op W)) {S : Sieve W} (hS : S ∈ J W)
    (h : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), S g → Presheaf.imageSieve φ (Q.map g.op y) ∈ J V) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve φ y ∈ J W :=
  J.transitive hS _ fun _ g hg => by
    rw [Presheaf.pullback_imageSieve]
    exact h g hg

/-- If a section is, on a covering sieve, in the image of a morphism, then that morphism is
locally surjective at it. -/
private lemma imageSieve_mem_of_exists {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ : P ⟶ Q) {W : C}
    (y : Q.obj (op W)) {S : Sieve W} (hS : S ∈ J W)
    (h : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), S g → ∃ t : P.obj (op V), φ.app (op V) t = Q.map g.op y) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve φ y ∈ J W :=
  J.superset_covering (fun _ g hg => h g hg) hS

end Sheaf

/-! ### The terminal sheaf of sets -/

section Terminal

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- The terminal sheaf of sets has exactly one section over every object of the site: the
underlying presheaf is terminal, because taking the underlying presheaf and evaluating at an
object both preserve limits. -/
@[instance_reducible,
  sga "4 VI 7.4.13.5" "special case"]
private noncomputable def uniqueTerminalObj (W : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Unique ((⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W) := by
  refine Types.isTerminalEquivUnique _ ?_
  exact
    terminalIsTerminal.isTerminalObj
      (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v) ⋙ (evaluation Cᵒᵖ (Type max u v)).obj W) _

/-- The section of the terminal sheaf of sets over an object. -/
private noncomputable def terminalSection (W : Cᵒᵖ) : (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W := by
  letI := uniqueTerminalObj (J := J) W
  exact default

/-- Two sections of the terminal sheaf of sets over the same object are equal. -/
private lemma terminal_eq {W : Cᵒᵖ} (x y : (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W) : x = y := by
  let := uniqueTerminalObj (J := J) W
  exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- A family of sections of a sheaf of sets compatible with restriction is a morphism from the
terminal sheaf: the terminal sheaf has exactly one section over every object, on which the
morphism takes the value of the family. -/
private noncomputable def homOfSections {G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (τ : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, G.obj.obj W)
    (hτ : ∀ (W W' : Cᵒᵖ) (f : W ⟶ W'), G.obj.map f (τ W) = τ W') :
    ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ G :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk
    { app := fun W => ↾fun _ => τ W
      naturality := fun W W' f => by
        refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun _ => ?_
        simp only [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, TypeCat.ofHom_apply]
        exact (hτ W W' f).symm }

private lemma homOfSections_app {G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (τ : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, G.obj.obj W)
    (hτ : ∀ (W W' : Cᵒᵖ) (f : W ⟶ W'), G.obj.map f (τ W) = τ W') (W : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W) : (homOfSections τ hτ).hom.app W x = τ W :=
  rfl

/-- A section of `G` singled out over every object by a property stable under restriction is a
global section: the property determines the family of sections uniquely, and that is what makes it
compatible with restriction. -/
private lemma exists_hom_terminal_of_existsUnique {G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    {Q : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, G.obj.obj W → Prop} (hQ : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, ∃! t : G.obj.obj W, Q W t)
    (hres : ∀ ⦃W W' : Cᵒᵖ⦄ (f : W ⟶ W') {t : G.obj.obj W}, Q W t → Q W' (G.obj.map f t)) :
    ∃ σ : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ G,
      ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W), Q W (σ.hom.app W x) := by
  choose τ hτ huniq using hQ
  refine ⟨homOfSections τ fun W W' f => huniq W' _ (hres f (hτ W)), fun W x => ?_⟩
  rw [homOfSections_app]
  exact hτ W

/-- **The constant sheaf at a singleton is a terminal sheaf**: the constant presheaf at a terminal
object is a sheaf and is terminal among presheaves, sheafification does not change it, and
`CategoryTheory.sheafToPresheaf` is fully faithful. -/
private noncomputable def isTerminalConstantSheaf (X : Type max u v) [Unique X] :
    IsTerminal ((constantSheaf J (Type max u v)).obj X) :=
  let hX : IsTerminal X := (Types.isTerminalEquivUnique X).symm inferInstance
  (Sheaf.isTerminalTerminal J hX).ofIso
    ((fullyFaithfulSheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v)).preimageIso
      (isoSheafify J (Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isTerminal J hX)))

/-- The terminal sheaf of sets is the constant sheaf at a singleton. -/
private noncomputable def constantSheafIsoTerminal (X : Type max u v) [Unique X] :
    (constantSheaf J (Type max u v)).obj X ≅ ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :=
  (isTerminalConstantSheaf X).uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal

end Terminal

/-! ### Sections of a binary product -/

section Prod

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- A pair of sections over `W` of two sheaves of sets comes from a section of their product:
the underlying presheaf of a product is the product of the underlying presheaves, and limits of
presheaves are computed objectwise. -/
lemma exists_prod_section (X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)) (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W)
    (y : Y.obj.obj W) :
    ∃ z : (X ⨯ Y).obj.obj W,
      (Limits.prod.fst : X ⨯ Y ⟶ X).hom.app W z = x ∧
        (Limits.prod.snd : X ⨯ Y ⟶ Y).hom.app W z = y := by
  obtain ⟨l, h₁, h₂⟩ :=
    BinaryFan.IsLimit.lift'
      (isLimitOfHasBinaryProductOfPreservesLimit
        (sheafToPresheaf J (Type max u v) ⋙ (evaluation Cᵒᵖ (Type max u v)).obj W) X Y)
      (↾fun _ : PUnit.{max u v + 1} => x) (↾fun _ : PUnit.{max u v + 1} => y)
  refine ⟨l PUnit.unit, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simpa using ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h₁ PUnit.unit
  · simpa using ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h₂ PUnit.unit

/-- A morphism out of `K` whose two composites with the projections of `K ⨯ K` agree takes the same
value on any two sections over the same object: the two sections come from a section of `K ⨯ K`. -/
private lemma apply_eq_apply_of_prod_fst_comp_eq {K G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {u : K ⟶ G}
    (hu : (Limits.prod.fst : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ u = (Limits.prod.snd : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ u) (W : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x y : K.obj.obj W) : u.hom.app W x = u.hom.app W y := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz₁, hz₂⟩ := exists_prod_section K K W x y
  rw [← hz₁, ← hz₂, ← comp_app_apply Limits.prod.fst u, ← comp_app_apply Limits.prod.snd u, hu]

end Prod

/-! ### Sheaves with local sections -/

section LocalSections

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- **Base change of a locally surjective morphism of sheaves of sets.**  If `G` surjects onto
the terminal sheaf, then the second projection `G ⨯ K ⟶ K` is surjective for every `K`: a section
of `K` over `W` is paired, over the objects where `G` has a section, with such a section. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_prod_snd {G K : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hG : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G)) :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.prod.snd : G ⨯ K ⟶ K) := by
  constructor
  intro W x
  refine
    imageSieve_mem_of_exists (Limits.prod.snd : G ⨯ K ⟶ K).hom x
      (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (terminal.from G).hom (terminalSection (op W))) fun V g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, -⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨z, -, hz⟩ := exists_prod_section G K (op V) y (K.obj.map g.op x)
  exact ⟨z, hz⟩

/-- A morphism `u : K ⟶ G` of sheaves of sets out of a sheaf which surjects onto the terminal sheaf
and whose two composites with the projections of `K ⨯ K` agree factors through the terminal sheaf,
that is, it is the restriction of a global section of `G`. The source phrases the hypothesis as
`K ⨯ K ⇉ K ⟶ *` being a coequalizer; only this equality and the surjectivity are used.

The value of that global section over `W` is characterised by taking, on every object over `W`
where `K` has a section, the value of `u` on it; the local values glue because `u` takes the same
value on any two sections over the same object, and the characterisation determines them uniquely,
which is what makes them natural. -/
private lemma exists_hom_terminal_of_prod_fst_comp_eq {K G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hK : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K)) {u : K ⟶ G}
    (hu : (Limits.prod.fst : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ u = (Limits.prod.snd : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ u) :
    ∃ σ : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ G, terminal.from K ≫ σ = u := by
  have hconst := apply_eq_apply_of_prod_fst_comp_eq hu
  have hcov : ∀ W : C, Presheaf.imageSieve (terminal.from K).hom (terminalSection (op W)) ∈ J W :=
    fun W => Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (terminal.from K).hom (terminalSection (op W))
  -- Over every object there is exactly one section taking, on the sections of `K` over the objects
  -- above it, the value of `u`; it exists because those values glue, `u` being constant.
  have key :
    ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ,
      ∃! t : G.obj.obj W,
        ∀ (V : C) (g : V ⟶ W.unop) (x : K.obj.obj (op V)),
          G.obj.map g.op t = u.hom.app (op V) x := by
    rintro ⟨W⟩
    have hglue :=
      exists_glue G.property (hcov W)
        (fun V g hg =>
          u.hom.app (op V)
            (Presheaf.localPreimage (terminal.from K).hom (terminalSection (op W)) g hg))
        (by
          intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ _
          rw [←
            NatTrans.naturality_apply u.hom g₁.op
              (Presheaf.localPreimage (terminal.from K).hom (terminalSection (op W)) f₁ h₁),
            ←
            NatTrans.naturality_apply u.hom g₂.op
              (Presheaf.localPreimage (terminal.from K).hom (terminalSection (op W)) f₂ h₂)]
          exact hconst (op Z) _ _)
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hglue
    have htv :
      ∀ (V : C) (g : V ⟶ W) (x : K.obj.obj (op V)), G.obj.map g.op t = u.hom.app (op V) x :=
      fun V g x => (ht g ⟨x, terminal_eq _ _⟩).trans (hconst (op V) _ _)
    refine ⟨t, htv, fun t' ht' => sheaf_ext G.property (hcov W) fun V g hg => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨x, -⟩ := hg
    rw [ht' V g x, htv V g x]
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ :=
    exists_hom_terminal_of_existsUnique key
      (by
        intro W W' f t ht V g x
        exact
          (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (G.obj.map_comp f g.op) t).symm.trans (ht V (g ≫ f.unop) x))
  refine ⟨σ, hom_ext_sections fun W z => ?_⟩
  simpa using hσ W ((terminal.from K).hom.app W z) W.unop (𝟙 W.unop) z

end LocalSections

/-! ### Global sections and the terminal sheaf -/

section GlobalSections

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- **Global sections are the morphisms from the terminal sheaf**, which is how the source defines
`Γ(C, ℱ)`: Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.ΓObjEquivHom` identifies them with the morphisms from
the constant sheaf at a singleton, and that sheaf is terminal. -/
private noncomputable def ΓEquivHom (G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :
    (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).obj G ≃ (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ G) :=
  (G.ΓObjEquivHom J PUnit.{max u v + 1}).trans
    ((constantSheafIsoTerminal PUnit.{max u v + 1}).homCongr (Iso.refl G))

/-- The identification of global sections with morphisms from the terminal sheaf is natural in the
sheaf: this is what turns a statement about `Ψ` into a statement about morphisms out of `⊤_`. -/
private lemma ΓEquivHom_naturality {G G' : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (f : G ⟶ G')
    (t : (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).obj G) :
    ΓEquivHom G' ((Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map f t) = ΓEquivHom G t ≫ f := by
  simp [ΓEquivHom, Sheaf.ΓObjEquivHom_naturality]

end GlobalSections

/-! ### The comparison map from the colimit of the underlying presheaves -/

section Comparison

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Λ : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} Λ]
  [HasColimitsOfShape Λ (Type max u v)] (D : Λ ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v))

end Comparison

section ComparisonFiltered

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Λ : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} Λ]
  [IsFiltered Λ] [HasColimitsOfShape Λ (Type max u v)] (D : Λ ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v))

end ComparisonFiltered

/-! ### Subfunctors of a sheaf of sets -/

section Subsheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- Sheafification of subfunctors is monotone. -/
private lemma sheafify_mono {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} {A B : Subfunctor P} (h : A ≤ B) :
    A.sheafify J ≤ B.sheafify J := fun _ _ hy => J.superset_covering (fun _ _g hg => h _ hg) hy

/-- Being locally in the image of a morphism is being in the sheafification of its range. -/
lemma mem_sheafify_range_iff {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ : P ⟶ Q) {W : C}
    (y : Q.obj (op W)) :
    y ∈ ((Subfunctor.range φ).sheafify J).obj (op W) ↔ Presheaf.imageSieve φ y ∈ J W :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The preimage of the sheafification of a subfunctor of a sheaf is closed under the local
condition, hence is a subsheaf. -/
private lemma preimage_sheafify_isSheaf {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (p : X ⟶ Y)
    (A : Subfunctor Y.obj) : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (((A.sheafify J).preimage p.hom)).toFunctor := by
  refine
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).2
      ((Subfunctor.isSheaf_iff _ ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J X.obj).1 X.property)).2
        fun W x hx => ?_)
  -- the sieve on which a section lies in the preimage is the one on which its image lies in `A`
  have hle :
    ((A.sheafify J).preimage p.hom).sieveOfSection x ≤
      (A.sheafify J).sieveOfSection (p.hom.app W x) :=
    fun V g hg => by
    rw [Subfunctor.sieveOfSection_apply, ← NatTrans.naturality_apply p.hom g.op x]
    rw [Subfunctor.sieveOfSection_apply, Subfunctor.preimage_obj, Set.mem_preimage] at hg
    exact hg
  have h : p.hom.app W x ∈ ((A.sheafify J).sheafify J).obj W := J.superset_covering hle hx
  rw [A.sheafify_sheafify ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J Y.obj).1 Y.property)] at h
  exact h

/-- A subfunctor of the underlying presheaf of a sheaf which is a sheaf, as a sheaf. -/
private def subsheaf {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (A : Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J A.toFunctor) : Sheaf J (Type max u v) :=
  ⟨A.toFunctor, hA⟩

/-- The inclusion of a subsheaf. -/
private def subsheafι {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (A : Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J A.toFunctor) : subsheaf A hA ⟶ X :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk A.ι

private lemma subsheafι_app_mem {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (A : Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J A.toFunctor) {W : Cᵒᵖ} (σ : (subsheaf A hA).obj.obj W) :
    (subsheafι A hA).hom.app W σ ∈ A.obj W :=
  σ.2

/-- The inclusion of a subsheaf is locally surjective at every section belonging to it: such a
section is in its image already over the maximal sieve. -/
private lemma imageSieve_subsheafι_mem {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (A : Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J A.toFunctor) {W : C} (x : X.obj.obj (op W)) (hx : x ∈ A.obj (op W)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve (subsheafι A hA).hom x ∈ J W :=
  imageSieve_mem_of_exists (subsheafι A hA).hom x (J.top_mem W) fun _V g _ =>
    ⟨(subsheaf A hA).obj.map g.op ⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩

end Subsheaf

/-! ### Quasi-compact sheaves of sets -/

section QuasiCompact

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- The value of the map from a coproduct on a section of one of the summands. -/
private lemma sigmaDesc_ι_app_apply {α : Type max u v} {G : α → Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    {Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (f : ∀ a, G a ⟶ Y) (a : α) (W : Cᵒᵖ) (σ : (G a).obj.obj W) :
    (Limits.Sigma.desc f).hom.app W ((Limits.Sigma.ι G a).hom.app W σ) = (f a).hom.app W σ := by
  rw [← comp_app_apply, Sigma.ι_comp_desc]

/-- A section in the image of one member of a family is in the image of the map from the
coproduct. -/
private lemma imageSieve_sigmaDesc_le {α : Type max u v} {G : α → Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    {Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (f : ∀ a, G a ⟶ Y) (a : α) {W : C} (y : Y.obj.obj (op W)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve (f a).hom y ≤ Presheaf.imageSieve (Limits.Sigma.desc f).hom y := by
  rintro V g ⟨σ, hσ⟩
  exact ⟨(Limits.Sigma.ι G a).hom.app (op V) σ, (sigmaDesc_ι_app_apply f a (op V) σ).trans hσ⟩

/-- The map from a coproduct of sheaves of sets is locally surjective as soon as every section of
the target is, locally, in the image of one of the members. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc {α : Type max u v} {G : α → Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    {Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (f : ∀ a, G a ⟶ Y)
    (h :
      ∀ (W : C) (y : Y.obj.obj (op W)),
        ∃ S ∈ J W,
          ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W),
            S g →
              ∃ (a : α) (σ : (G a).obj.obj (op V)), (f a).hom.app (op V) σ = Y.obj.map g.op y) :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc f) := by
  constructor
  intro W y
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ := h W y
  refine imageSieve_mem_of_exists (Limits.Sigma.desc f).hom y hS fun V g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, σ, hσ⟩ := hloc g hg
  exact imageSieve_sigmaDesc_le f a y g ⟨σ, hσ⟩

/-- A section of a coproduct of sheaves of sets is, locally, in the image of one of the
summands. -/
private lemma exists_local_summand {α : Type max u v} (G : α → Sheaf J (Type max u v)) (W : C)
    (z : (∐ G).obj.obj (op W)) :
    ∃ S ∈ J W,
      ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W),
        S g →
          ∃ (a : α) (σ : (G a).obj.obj (op V)),
            (Limits.Sigma.ι G a).hom.app (op V) σ = (∐ G).obj.map g.op z := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ :=
    Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.exists_local_section (Discrete.functor G) W z
  refine ⟨S, hS, fun V g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨a⟩, σ, hσ⟩ := hloc g hg
  exact ⟨a, σ, hσ⟩

end QuasiCompact

/-! ### The subsheaf of sections lying locally in the image of a morphism -/

section PreimageRange

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {X Y Z : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (p : X ⟶ Y) (φ : Z ⟶ Y)

/-- The subsheaf of `X` of the sections whose image under `p` lies locally in the image of `φ`,
that is, the preimage under `p` of the image sheaf of `φ`. -/
private def preimageRange : Subfunctor X.obj :=
  ((Subfunctor.range φ.hom).sheafify J).preimage p.hom

private lemma mem_preimageRange_iff {W : C} (x : X.obj.obj (op W)) :
    x ∈ (preimageRange p φ).obj (op W) ↔ Presheaf.imageSieve φ.hom (p.hom.app (op W) x) ∈ J W :=
  mem_sheafify_range_iff φ.hom (p.hom.app (op W) x)

/-- A section whose image under `p` is in the image of `φ` lies in `preimageRange p φ`. -/
private lemma mem_preimageRange_of_apply_eq {W : C} (x : X.obj.obj (op W)) (t : Z.obj.obj (op W))
    (h : φ.hom.app (op W) t = p.hom.app (op W) x) : x ∈ (preimageRange p φ).obj (op W) := by
  rw [mem_preimageRange_iff, ← h, Presheaf.imageSieve_app]
  exact J.top_mem _

private lemma preimageRange_isSheaf : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (preimageRange p φ).toFunctor :=
  preimage_sheafify_isSheaf p _

/-- `preimageRange p φ` as a sheaf of sets. -/
private def preimageRangeSheaf : Sheaf J (Type max u v) :=
  subsheaf _ (preimageRange_isSheaf p φ)

/-- The inclusion of `preimageRangeSheaf p φ` into `X`. -/
private def preimageRangeι : preimageRangeSheaf p φ ⟶ X :=
  subsheafι _ (preimageRange_isSheaf p φ)

private lemma preimageRangeι_app_mem {W : Cᵒᵖ} (σ : (preimageRangeSheaf p φ).obj.obj W) :
    (preimageRangeι p φ).hom.app W σ ∈ (preimageRange p φ).obj W :=
  subsheafι_app_mem (preimageRange p φ) (preimageRange_isSheaf p φ) σ

/-- The inclusion of `preimageRangeSheaf p φ` is locally surjective at every section belonging
to `preimageRange p φ`. -/
private lemma imageSieve_preimageRangeι_mem {W : C} (x : X.obj.obj (op W))
    (hx : x ∈ (preimageRange p φ).obj (op W)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve (preimageRangeι p φ).hom x ∈ J W :=
  imageSieve_subsheafι_mem (preimageRange p φ) (preimageRange_isSheaf p φ) x hx

/-- Enlarging `φ` along a morphism over `Y` enlarges the subsheaf. -/
private lemma preimageRange_mono {Z' : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (φ' : Z' ⟶ Y) (ψ : Z ⟶ Z')
    (hψ : ψ ≫ φ' = φ) : preimageRange p φ ≤ preimageRange p φ' := by
  have hle : Subfunctor.range φ.hom ≤ Subfunctor.range φ'.hom := by
    rintro U y ⟨t, ht⟩
    exact ⟨ψ.hom.app U t, (comp_app_apply ψ φ' U t).symm.trans ((congr_app_apply hψ U t).trans ht)⟩
  intro W x hx
  rw [preimageRange, Subfunctor.preimage_obj, Set.mem_preimage] at hx ⊢
  exact Set.mem_of_subset_of_mem (sheafify_mono hle W) hx

end PreimageRange

section QuasiCompactTransfer

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- For a morphism `p : X ⟶ Y` and a family `f a : G a ⟶ Y`, a section of `X` lies locally in the
image of the coproduct of the subsheaves `preimageRangeSheaf p (f a)` exactly when it lies in
`preimageRange p (∐ f)`, that is, when its image under `p` lies locally in the image of the
coproduct of the `f a`.

Both directions come from the same computation: a local section of the coproduct lies in one
summand (`exists_local_summand`), and there `preimageRangeι p (f a)` and `f a` say the same thing
about the restriction of the section. -/
private lemma imageSieve_sigmaDesc_preimageRangeι_mem_iff {α : Type max u v}
    {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (p : X ⟶ Y) {G : α → Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (f : ∀ a, G a ⟶ Y)
    {W : C} (x : X.obj.obj (op W)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve (Limits.Sigma.desc fun a => preimageRangeι p (f a)).hom x ∈ J W ↔
      x ∈ (preimageRange p (Limits.Sigma.desc f)).obj (op W) := by
  rw [mem_preimageRange_iff]
  constructor
  · refine fun hx => imageSieve_mem_of_local _ _ hx fun V g hg => ?_
    obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ := hg
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ := exists_local_summand (fun a => preimageRangeSheaf p (f a)) V ζ
    refine imageSieve_mem_of_local _ _ hS fun Z' q hq => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, τ, hτ⟩ := hloc q hq
    have hmem : X.obj.map q.op (X.obj.map g.op x) ∈ (preimageRange p (f a)).obj (op Z') := by
      have e : (preimageRangeι p (f a)).hom.app (op Z') τ = X.obj.map q.op (X.obj.map g.op x) := by
        rw [← sigmaDesc_ι_app_apply (fun a => preimageRangeι p (f a)) a (op Z') τ, hτ,
          NatTrans.naturality_apply (Limits.Sigma.desc fun a => preimageRangeι p (f a)).hom q.op ζ,
          hζ]
      exact e ▸ preimageRangeι_app_mem p (f a) τ
    rw [mem_preimageRange_iff, naturality_apply₂ p q g x] at hmem
    exact J.superset_covering (imageSieve_sigmaDesc_le f a _) hmem
  · refine fun hx => imageSieve_mem_of_local _ x hx fun V g hg => ?_
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hg
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ := exists_local_summand G V z
    refine imageSieve_mem_of_local _ (X.obj.map g.op x) hS fun Z' q hq => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, σ, hσ⟩ := hloc q hq
    have hpx :
      (f a).hom.app (op Z') σ = p.hom.app (op Z') (X.obj.map q.op (X.obj.map g.op x)) := by
      rw [naturality_apply₂ p q g x, ← hz, ←
        NatTrans.naturality_apply (Limits.Sigma.desc f).hom q.op z, ← hσ, sigmaDesc_ι_app_apply]
    exact
      J.superset_covering (imageSieve_sigmaDesc_le (fun a => preimageRangeι p (f a)) a _)
        (imageSieve_preimageRangeι_mem p (f a) _ (mem_preimageRange_of_apply_eq p (f a) _ σ hpx))

/-- **Stacks 0GMP.** A sheaf of sets which receives a surjection from a quasi-compact sheaf is
quasi-compact.

Given a surjection `∐_a G a ⟶ Y`, the subsheaves `preimageRangeSheaf p (f a)` of `X` cover `X`, so
finitely many of them already do; the same equivalence then says that the corresponding `f a` still
cover `Y`. -/
private lemma isQuasiCompact_of_isLocallySurjective {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (p : X ⟶ Y)
    [Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective p] (hX : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact X) : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact Y := by
  intro α G f hf
  have hν : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc fun a : α => preimageRangeι p (f a)) := by
    constructor
    intro W x
    exact
      (imageSieve_sigmaDesc_preimageRangeι_mem_iff p f x).2
        ((mem_preimageRange_iff p _ x).2 (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J _ _))
  obtain ⟨T, hTfin, hT⟩ :=
    hX α (fun a => preimageRangeSheaf p (f a)) (fun a => preimageRangeι p (f a)) hν
  refine ⟨T, hTfin, ?_⟩
  constructor
  intro W y
  refine imageSieve_mem_of_local _ y (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J p.hom y) fun V g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hg
  rw [← hx]
  exact
    (imageSieve_sigmaDesc_preimageRangeι_mem_iff p (fun j : T => f j.1) x).1
      (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J _ x)

/-- The hypothesis of part (4) of the source makes the topos quasi-compact: it produces a sheaf
`K₀` surjecting onto the terminal sheaf with `K₀ ⨯ K₀` quasi-compact, and `prod.snd : K₀ ⨯ K₀ ⟶ K₀`
is surjective, so `K₀` is quasi-compact, and then so is the terminal sheaf. Both steps are Stacks
0GMP. -/
private lemma isQuasiCompact_terminal_of_covering_set {S : Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v))}
    (hSa :
      ∀ G : Sheaf J (Type max u v),
        Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G) →
          ∃ K ∈ S, Nonempty (K ⟶ G) ∧ Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K))
    (hSb : ∀ K ∈ S, Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact (K ⨯ K)) :
    Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))) := by
  obtain ⟨K₀, hK₀S, -, hK₀surj⟩ :=
    hSa _
      (by
        rw [terminal.hom_ext (terminal.from (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)))) (𝟙 _)]
        infer_instance)
  have := hK₀surj
  have := isLocallySurjective_prod_snd (K := K₀) hK₀surj
  exact
    isQuasiCompact_of_isLocallySurjective (terminal.from K₀)
      (isQuasiCompact_of_isLocallySurjective (Limits.prod.snd : K₀ ⨯ K₀ ⟶ K₀) (hSb K₀ hK₀S))

end QuasiCompactTransfer

/-! ### Directed families of subsheaves of a quasi-compact sheaf -/

section Engine

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- A subsheaf whose inclusion is locally surjective is the whole sheaf: every section of the
ambient sheaf is then locally in it, and a subsheaf is closed under that. -/
private lemma mem_of_isLocallySurjective_subsheafι {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (A : Subfunctor X.obj) (hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J A.toFunctor)
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (subsheafι A hA).hom] (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W) :
    x ∈ A.obj W := by
  refine
    (A.isSheaf_iff ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J X.obj).1 X.property)).1
      ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).1 hA) W x
      (J.superset_covering ?_ (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (subsheafι A hA).hom x))
  rintro V g ⟨σ, hσ⟩
  have hmem := subsheafι_app_mem A hA σ
  rw [hσ] at hmem
  exact hmem

/-- If the coproduct of a family of subsheaves all contained in a subsheaf `B` surjects onto the
ambient sheaf, then the inclusion of `B` is locally surjective: the map from the coproduct factors
through it. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_subsheafι_of_le {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {γ : Type max u v}
    (A : γ → Subfunctor X.obj) (hsheaf : ∀ c, Presheaf.IsSheaf J (A c).toFunctor)
    {B : Subfunctor X.obj} (hB : Presheaf.IsSheaf J B.toFunctor) (hle : ∀ c, A c ≤ B)
    (h : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc fun c => subsheafι (A c) (hsheaf c))) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (subsheafι B hB).hom := by
  have := h
  have hfacS :
    (Limits.Sigma.desc fun c =>
          (ObjectProperty.homMk (Subfunctor.homOfLe (hle c)) :
            subsheaf (A c) (hsheaf c) ⟶ subsheaf B hB)) ≫
        subsheafι B hB =
      Limits.Sigma.desc fun c => subsheafι (A c) (hsheaf c) := by
    refine Limits.Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun c => ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, Sigma.ι_comp_desc, Sigma.ι_comp_desc]
    exact Sheaf.hom_ext (Subfunctor.homOfLe_ι (hle c))
  exact
    Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac J
      (congrArg (fun ff : (∐ fun c => subsheaf (A c) (hsheaf c)) ⟶ X => ff.hom) hfacS)

/-- **The quasi-compactness engine**, for a family indexed by a type in `Type max u v`, where the
coproduct of the family exists: a family of subsheaves of a quasi-compact sheaf of sets which is
directed (every finite subfamily has an upper bound) and covers every section locally contains a
member which is the whole sheaf.

The map from the coproduct of the family is locally surjective, so already the coproduct of a
finite subfamily surjects onto the sheaf; an upper bound of that subfamily then contains every
section locally, hence contains it. -/
private lemma exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact' {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hX : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact X) {β : Type max u v} (A : β → Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hsheaf : ∀ b, Presheaf.IsSheaf J (A b).toFunctor)
    (hdir : ∀ T : Set β, T.Finite → ∃ b, ∀ c ∈ T, A c ≤ A b)
    (hcov :
      ∀ (W : C) (x : X.obj.obj (op W)),
        ∃ S ∈ J W, ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), S g → ∃ b, X.obj.map g.op x ∈ (A b).obj (op V)) :
    ∃ b, ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), x ∈ (A b).obj W := by
  classical
  have hsurj :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Limits.Sigma.desc fun b : β => subsheafι (A b) (hsheaf b)) := by
    refine isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc _ fun W x => ?_
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ := hcov W x
    refine ⟨S, hS, fun V g hg => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hloc g hg
    exact ⟨b, ⟨X.obj.map g.op x, hb⟩, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨T, hTfin, hT⟩ :=
    hX β (fun b => subsheaf (A b) (hsheaf b)) (fun b => subsheafι (A b) (hsheaf b)) hsurj
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hdir T hTfin
  have :=
    isLocallySurjective_subsheafι_of_le (fun c : T => A c.1) (fun c => hsheaf c.1) (hsheaf b)
      (fun c => hb c.1 c.2) hT
  exact ⟨b, mem_of_isLocallySurjective_subsheafι (A b) (hsheaf b)⟩

/-- **The quasi-compactness engine.** A directed family of subsheaves of a quasi-compact sheaf of
sets which covers every section locally contains a member which is the whole sheaf.

The index type is arbitrary, while the coproduct of `exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact'` is indexed by a
type in `Type max u v`: the family is therefore reindexed by the subfunctors it consists of, and
`Subfunctor X.obj` is such a type. This is what stands in for the source's coproduct `∐_{i ∈ I}`
over the index category of a filtered diagram, which need not exist in `Sheaf J (Type max u v)`. -/
private lemma exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hX : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact X) {β : Type*} (A : β → Subfunctor X.obj)
    (hsheaf : ∀ b, Presheaf.IsSheaf J (A b).toFunctor)
    (hdir : ∀ T : Set β, T.Finite → ∃ b, ∀ c ∈ T, A c ≤ A b)
    (hcov :
      ∀ (W : C) (x : X.obj.obj (op W)),
        ∃ S ∈ J W, ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), S g → ∃ b, X.obj.map g.op x ∈ (A b).obj (op V)) :
    ∃ b, ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), x ∈ (A b).obj W := by
  classical
  suffices h :
    ∃ B : ↥(Set.range A), ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), x ∈ (B : Subfunctor X.obj).obj W
    by
    obtain ⟨⟨B, b, rfl⟩, hB⟩ := h
    exact ⟨b, hB⟩
  refine
    exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact' hX (fun B : ↥(Set.range A) => (B : Subfunctor X.obj)) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro ⟨B, b, rfl⟩
    exact hsheaf b
  · intro T hT
    choose bb hbb using fun c : ↥(Set.range A) => c.2
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hdir (bb '' T) (hT.image bb)
    refine ⟨⟨A b, b, rfl⟩, fun c hc => ?_⟩
    rw [← hbb c]
    exact hb _ ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩
  · intro W x
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ := hcov W x
    refine ⟨S, hS, fun V g hg => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hloc g hg
    exact ⟨⟨A b, b, rfl⟩, hb⟩

/-- The subfunctor of the sections on which two morphisms of presheaves agree. -/
private def eqSub {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ ψ : X.obj ⟶ P) :
    Subfunctor X.obj
    where
  obj W := {x | φ.app W x = ψ.app W x}
  map i x hx := by
    rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hx
    rw [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
    rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply φ i x, NatTrans.naturality_apply ψ i x]
    exact congrArg (P.map i) hx

/-- Membership in `eqSub φ ψ` is agreement of the two morphisms. -/
private lemma mem_eqSub {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (φ ψ : X.obj ⟶ P)
    {W : Cᵒᵖ} (x : X.obj.obj W) : x ∈ (eqSub φ ψ).obj W ↔ φ.app W x = ψ.app W x :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Postcomposing both morphisms with a third one enlarges the subfunctor where they agree. -/
private lemma eqSub_le_comp {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v}
    (φ ψ : X.obj ⟶ P) (χ : P ⟶ Q) : eqSub φ ψ ≤ eqSub (φ ≫ χ) (ψ ≫ χ) := fun W _ hx =>
  congrArg (χ.app W) hx

/-- Where two morphisms into a sheaf agree is a subsheaf: a sheaf of sets is separated. -/
private lemma eqSub_isSheaf {X Y : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (φ ψ : X.obj ⟶ Y.obj) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J (eqSub φ ψ).toFunctor := by
  refine
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).2
      ((Subfunctor.isSheaf_iff _ ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J X.obj).1 X.property)).2
        fun W x hx => ?_)
  rw [mem_eqSub]
  refine sheaf_ext Y.property hx fun V g hg => ?_
  rw [← NatTrans.naturality_apply φ g.op x, ← NatTrans.naturality_apply ψ g.op x]
  exact hg

end Engine

/-! ### The comparison map on global sections -/

section Main

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I]
  [IsFiltered I] [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)] (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v))

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- `Ψ` is described by the components of the colimit cocone of `F`. -/
private lemma post_Γ_ι (i : I) (t : (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).obj (F.obj i)) :
    colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) (colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i t) =
      (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (colimit.ι F i) t :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (colimit.ι_post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i) t

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- A global section of `F i` and its image in `F k` have the same image in the colimit of global
sections. -/
private lemma ι_Γ_map {i k : I} (w : i ⟶ k) (t : (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).obj (F.obj i)) :
    colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) k ((Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (F.map w) t) =
      colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i t :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (colimit.w (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) w) t

/-- `Ψ` is injective as soon as two morphisms from the terminal sheaf to some `F i` with the same
composition with `colimit.ι F i` become equal after a transition map: a filtered colimit of sets is
separated as soon as it is separated on each member of the diagram. -/
private lemma injective_post_Γ_of_exists
    (hcore :
      ∀ (i : I) (φ ψ : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ F.obj i),
        φ ≫ colimit.ι F i = ψ ≫ colimit.ι F i → ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k), φ ≫ F.map w = ψ ≫ F.map w) :
    Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) := by
  intro x y hxy
  obtain ⟨i, a, b, ha, hb⟩ :=
    Types.FilteredColimit.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit₂
      (colimit.isColimit (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) x y
  have ha' : colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i a = x := ha
  have hb' : colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i b = y := hb
  subst ha'
  subst hb'
  have key :
    (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (colimit.ι F i) a =
      (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (colimit.ι F i) b :=
    (post_Γ_ι F i a).symm.trans (hxy.trans (post_Γ_ι F i b))
  obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ :=
    hcore i (ΓEquivHom (F.obj i) a) (ΓEquivHom (F.obj i) b)
      (by rw [← ΓEquivHom_naturality, ← ΓEquivHom_naturality, key])
  have hab :
    (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (F.map w) a = (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)).map (F.map w) b :=
    (ΓEquivHom (F.obj k)).injective
      (by rwa [ΓEquivHom_naturality, ΓEquivHom_naturality])
  rw [← ι_Γ_map F w a, ← ι_Γ_map F w b, hab]

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- `Ψ` is surjective as soon as every morphism from the terminal sheaf to the colimit factors
through some `F i`. -/
private lemma surjective_post_Γ_of_exists
    (hcore :
      ∀ s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F,
        ∃ (i : I) (σ : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ F.obj i), σ ≫ colimit.ι F i = s) :
    Function.Surjective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) := by
  intro t
  obtain ⟨i, σ, hσ⟩ := hcore (ΓEquivHom (colimit F) t)
  refine
    ⟨colimit.ι (F ⋙ Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)) i ((ΓEquivHom (F.obj i)).symm σ),
      (post_Γ_ι F i _).trans ((ΓEquivHom (colimit F)).injective ?_)⟩
  rw [ΓEquivHom_naturality, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, hσ]

/-- Alias of `Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.injective_ι_app_of_mono`. -/
private alias injective_ι_app_of_mono :=
  Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.injective_ι_app_of_mono

/-- **Part (1)** of the source: injective transition maps make `Ψ` injective, no quasi-compactness
needed. Two morphisms from the terminal sheaf which agree in the colimit already agree, the maps to
the colimit sheaf being injective on sections. -/
private lemma injective_post_Γ_of_mono (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) :
    Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) := by
  refine injective_post_Γ_of_exists F fun i φ ψ h => ⟨i, 𝟙 i, ?_⟩
  rw [hom_ext_sections fun W z => injective_ι_app_of_mono F hmono W.unop i (congr_app_apply h W z)]

omit [IsFiltered I] [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type (max u v))] in
/-- The equalizer subsheaves of `φ` and `ψ` increase along the transition maps. -/
private lemma eqSub_mono {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} {i k k' : I} (φ ψ : X ⟶ F.obj i) (w : i ⟶ k)
    (v : k ⟶ k') :
    eqSub (φ ≫ F.map w).hom (ψ ≫ F.map w).hom ≤
      eqSub (φ ≫ F.map (w ≫ v)).hom (ψ ≫ F.map (w ≫ v)).hom := by
  rw [F.map_comp, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
  exact eqSub_le_comp (φ ≫ F.map w).hom (ψ ≫ F.map w).hom (F.map v).hom

/-- **Part (2)** of the source, in the form used by the other parts: two morphisms from a
quasi-compact sheaf to `F i` which agree in the colimit agree after a transition map.

The subsheaves on which the two morphisms agree after a transition map out of `i` form a directed
family, `I` being filtered, and it covers every section locally by `exists_local_transition`. -/
private lemma exists_transition_comp_eq {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (hX : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact X)
    (i : I) (φ ψ : X ⟶ F.obj i) (h : φ ≫ colimit.ι F i = ψ ≫ colimit.ι F i) :
    ∃ (k : I) (w : i ⟶ k), φ ≫ F.map w = ψ ≫ F.map w := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨⟨k, w⟩, hkw⟩ :
    ∃ kw : Σ k : I, i ⟶ k,
      ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), x ∈ (eqSub (φ ≫ F.map kw.2).hom (ψ ≫ F.map kw.2).hom).obj W :=
    by
    refine
      exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact hX
        (fun kw : Σ k : I, i ⟶ k => eqSub (φ ≫ F.map kw.2).hom (ψ ≫ F.map kw.2).hom)
        (fun _ => eqSub_isSheaf _ _) (fun T hT => ?_) (fun W x => ?_)
    · have : Finite ↥T := hT.to_subtype
      obtain ⟨k', w', v, hv⟩ :=
        exists_comp_eq_of_finite (I := I) i (fun c : ↥T => (c : Σ k : I, i ⟶ k).1)
          (fun c => (c : Σ k : I, i ⟶ k).2)
      refine ⟨⟨k', w'⟩, fun c hc => ?_⟩
      have h1 := eqSub_mono F φ ψ ((⟨c, hc⟩ : ↥T) : Σ k : I, i ⟶ k).2 (v ⟨c, hc⟩)
      rw [hv ⟨c, hc⟩] at h1
      exact h1
    · obtain ⟨S, hS, hloc⟩ :=
        Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.exists_local_transition F W i (φ.hom.app (op W) x)
          (ψ.hom.app (op W) x) (congr_app_apply h (op W) x)
      refine ⟨S, hS, fun V g hg => ?_⟩
      obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ := hloc g hg
      refine ⟨⟨k, w⟩, ?_⟩
      rw [mem_eqSub, ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom,
        ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, NatTrans.comp_app_apply, NatTrans.comp_app_apply,
        NatTrans.naturality_apply φ.hom g.op x, NatTrans.naturality_apply ψ.hom g.op x]
      exact hw
  exact ⟨k, w, hom_ext_sections fun W x => hkw W x⟩

/-- **Part (2)** of the source: `Ψ` is injective as soon as the terminal sheaf is quasi-compact,
that is, as soon as the topos is. -/
private lemma injective_post_Γ_of_isQuasiCompact
    (hT : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)))) :
    Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) :=
  injective_post_Γ_of_exists F fun i φ ψ h => exists_transition_comp_eq F hT i φ ψ h

/-- A morphism from a quasi-compact sheaf of sets to the colimit sheaf lands, locally, in the image
of one and the same member of the diagram: the subsheaves of sections whose image lies locally in
the image of `colimit.ι F i` form a directed family which covers every section locally.

This is the form in which the source's coproduct `∐_{i ∈ I}` is used; see the implementation
notes. -/
private lemma exists_forall_mem_preimageRange {X : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hX : Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact X) (s : X ⟶ colimit F) :
    ∃ i : I, ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj.obj W), x ∈ (preimageRange s (colimit.ι F i)).obj W := by
  classical
  refine
    exists_mem_of_isQuasiCompact hX (fun i => preimageRange s (colimit.ι F i))
      (fun _ => preimageRange_isSheaf _ _) (fun T hT => ?_) (fun W x => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := IsFiltered.sup_objs_exists hT.toFinset
    refine ⟨k, fun c hc => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨w⟩ := hk (hT.mem_toFinset.2 hc)
    exact preimageRange_mono s (colimit.ι F c) (colimit.ι F k) (F.map w) (colimit.w F w)
  · obtain ⟨S₀, hS₀, hloc⟩ :=
      Stacks.Sites.FilteredColimitSections.exists_local_section F W (s.hom.app (op W) x)
    refine ⟨S₀, hS₀, fun V g hg => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨l, t, ht⟩ := hloc g hg
    exact
      ⟨l,
        mem_preimageRange_of_apply_eq s (colimit.ι F l) _ t
          (ht.trans (NatTrans.naturality_apply s.hom g.op x).symm)⟩

/-- **Part (3)** of the source, surjectivity: for a quasi-compact topos and injective transition
maps, every morphism from the terminal sheaf to the colimit factors through some `F i`.

By `exists_forall_mem_preimageRange` the section `s` lies, over every object, locally in the image
of a single `colimit.ι F i`. Since the transition maps are monomorphisms that map is injective on
sections (`injective_ι_app_of_mono`), so the local preimages are unique and glue
(`exists_preimage_of_injective`) to a section over each object; uniqueness again makes those
sections natural, and the resulting morphism `σ : ⊤_ ⟶ F.obj i` satisfies
`σ ≫ colimit.ι F i = s` by construction. -/
private lemma exists_factor_of_isQuasiCompactTopos_of_mono (hQC : J.IsQuasiCompactTopos)
    (hmono : ∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f))
    (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) :
    ∃ (i : I) (σ : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ F.obj i), σ ≫ colimit.ι F i = s := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_forall_mem_preimageRange F hQC s
  have hinj : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, Function.Injective ((colimit.ι F i).hom.app W) := by
    rintro ⟨W⟩
    exact injective_ι_app_of_mono F hmono W i
  -- Over every object the local preimages of `s` are unique, hence glue to a single preimage.
  have key :
    ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ,
      ∃! x : (F.obj i).obj.obj W,
        (colimit.ι F i).hom.app W x = s.hom.app W (terminalSection W) := by
    rintro ⟨W⟩
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ :=
      exists_preimage_of_injective (colimit.ι F i) (fun V => hinj (op V)) _
        ((mem_preimageRange_iff s (colimit.ι F i) (terminalSection (op W))).1 (hi (op W) _))
    exact ⟨x, hx, fun y hy => hinj (op W) (hy.trans hx.symm)⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ :=
    exists_hom_terminal_of_existsUnique key
      (by
        intro W W' f x hx
        rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply (colimit.ι F i).hom f x, hx, ←
          NatTrans.naturality_apply s.hom f (terminalSection W)]
        exact congrArg (s.hom.app W') (terminal_eq _ _))
  exact
    ⟨i, σ, hom_ext_sections fun W z => (hσ W z).trans (congrArg (s.hom.app W) (terminal_eq _ z))⟩

/-- The fibre product `⊤_ ×_{s, colim F} F i` of a global section `s` of the colimit sheaf with the
`i`-th member of the diagram: it is the subfunctor of `F i` on which `colimit.ι F i` agrees with
the composition of `s` with the map to the terminal sheaf, because the terminal sheaf has exactly
one section over every object. -/
private noncomputable def fibSub (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) :
    Subfunctor (F.obj i).obj :=
  eqSub (colimit.ι F i).hom ((terminal.from (F.obj i) ≫ s).hom)

omit [IsFiltered I] in
private lemma fibSub_isSheaf (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J (fibSub F s i).toFunctor :=
  eqSub_isSheaf _ _

omit [IsFiltered I] in
private lemma mem_fibSub_iff (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) {W : Cᵒᵖ}
    (t : (F.obj i).obj.obj W) :
    t ∈ (fibSub F s i).obj W ↔ (colimit.ι F i).hom.app W t = s.hom.app W (terminalSection W) := by
  have e : ((terminal.from (F.obj i) ≫ s).hom).app W t = s.hom.app W (terminalSection W) :=
    congrArg (s.hom.app W) (terminal_eq _ _)
  rw [fibSub, mem_eqSub, e]

/-- `fibSub F s i` as a sheaf of sets. -/
private noncomputable def fibSheaf (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) :
    Sheaf J (Type max u v) :=
  subsheaf (fibSub F s i) (fibSub_isSheaf F s i)

/-- The inclusion of `fibSheaf F s i` into `F i`. -/
private noncomputable def fibι (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) :
    fibSheaf F s i ⟶ F.obj i :=
  subsheafι (fibSub F s i) (fibSub_isSheaf F s i)

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- The fibre product lies over `s`: its inclusion followed by `colimit.ι F i` is the restriction
of `s` along the map to the terminal sheaf. -/
private lemma fibι_comp_ι (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I) :
    fibι F s i ≫ colimit.ι F i = terminal.from (fibSheaf F s i) ≫ s := by
  refine hom_ext_sections fun W z => ?_
  rw [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom,
    NatTrans.comp_app_apply, NatTrans.comp_app_apply]
  have hmem : (fibι F s i).hom.app W z ∈ (fibSub F s i).obj W :=
    subsheafι_app_mem (fibSub F s i) (fibSub_isSheaf F s i) z
  rw [mem_fibSub_iff] at hmem
  rw [hmem]
  exact congrArg (s.hom.app W) (terminal_eq _ _)

omit [IsFiltered I] in
/-- If a global section `s` of the colimit sheaf lies, over every object, locally in the image of
`colimit.ι F i`, then the fibre product `⊤_ ×_{s, colim F} F i` surjects onto the terminal sheaf: a
local preimage of `s` under `colimit.ι F i` is a section of the fibre product. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_terminal_from_fibSheaf
    (s : ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) ⟶ colimit F) (i : I)
    (hi :
      ∀ (W : Cᵒᵖ) (x : (⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type max u v))).obj.obj W),
        x ∈ (preimageRange s (colimit.ι F i)).obj W) :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from (fibSheaf F s i)) := by
  constructor
  intro W x
  have hx := hi (op W) x
  rw [mem_preimageRange_iff] at hx
  refine imageSieve_mem_of_exists (terminal.from (fibSheaf F s i)).hom x hx fun V g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hg
  have hmem : t ∈ (fibSub F s i).obj (op V) := by
    rw [mem_fibSub_iff, ht, ← NatTrans.naturality_apply s.hom g.op x]
    exact congrArg (s.hom.app (op V)) (terminal_eq _ _)
  exact ⟨⟨t, hmem⟩, terminal_eq _ _⟩

/-- **Part (4)** of the source.

The hypothesis makes the topos quasi-compact (`isQuasiCompact_terminal_of_covering_set`), so
injectivity of `Ψ` is part (2).

For surjectivity, let `s : ⊤_ ⟶ colimit F` be a global section of the colimit. By
`exists_forall_mem_preimageRange` there is an `i₀` with `s` lying locally in the image of
`colimit.ι F i₀` over every object, so the fibre product `fibSheaf F s i₀` surjects onto the
terminal sheaf; applying (4)(a) to it produces `K ∈ S` with `K ⟶ ⊤_` surjective together with a
morphism `u : K ⟶ F i₀` satisfying `u ≫ colimit.ι F i₀ = terminal.from K ≫ s`. The two composites
`prod.fst ≫ u` and `prod.snd ≫ u` out of `K ⨯ K` then agree in the colimit, because both composites
`K ⨯ K ⟶ ⊤_` are the unique one, so part (2) applied to the quasi-compact `K ⨯ K` gives a
transition map `w : i₀ ⟶ k` with `prod.fst ≫ u ≫ F.map w = prod.snd ≫ u ≫ F.map w`. Thus
`u ≫ F.map w` takes the same value on any two sections over the same object
(`exists_prod_section`), hence descends to a global section `σ` of `F k` with
`terminal.from K ≫ σ = u ≫ F.map w` (`exists_hom_terminal_of_constant`), and
`σ ≫ colimit.ι F k = s` follows because `terminal.from K` is an epimorphism.

This differs from the source only in replacing the coproduct `∐_{i ∈ I}` of the fibre products by
the family of subsheaves of `exists_forall_mem_preimageRange`; see the implementation notes. -/
private lemma bijective_post_Γ_of_covering_set
    (hS :
      ∃ S : Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v)),
        (∀ G : Sheaf J (Type max u v),
            Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G) →
              ∃ K ∈ S, Nonempty (K ⟶ G) ∧ Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K)) ∧
          ∀ K ∈ S, Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact (K ⨯ K)) :
    Function.Bijective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v))) := by
  obtain ⟨S, hSa, hSb⟩ := hS
  have hTop := isQuasiCompact_terminal_of_covering_set hSa hSb
  refine ⟨injective_post_Γ_of_isQuasiCompact F hTop, surjective_post_Γ_of_exists F fun s => ?_⟩
  -- The index at which `s` is locally realised, and (4)(a) applied to the fibre product there.
  obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := exists_forall_mem_preimageRange F hTop s
  obtain ⟨K, hKS, ⟨u₀⟩, hKsurj⟩ := hSa _ (isLocallySurjective_terminal_from_fibSheaf F s i₀ hi₀)
  -- A morphism `K ⟶ F i₀` over `s`.
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ : ∃ u : K ⟶ F.obj i₀, u ≫ colimit.ι F i₀ = terminal.from K ≫ s :=
    ⟨u₀ ≫ fibι F s i₀, by
      rw [Category.assoc, fibι_comp_ι, ← Category.assoc,
        terminal.hom_ext (u₀ ≫ terminal.from (fibSheaf F s i₀)) (terminal.from K)]⟩
  -- The two projections of `K ⨯ K` agree in the colimit, hence after a transition map.
  have hab : (Limits.prod.fst ≫ u) ≫ colimit.ι F i₀ = (Limits.prod.snd ≫ u) ≫ colimit.ι F i₀ := by
    have h1 :
      (Limits.prod.fst : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ terminal.from K =
        (Limits.prod.snd : K ⨯ K ⟶ K) ≫ terminal.from K :=
      terminal.hom_ext _ _
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hu, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, h1]
  obtain ⟨k, w, hw⟩ :=
    exists_transition_comp_eq F (hSb K hKS) i₀ (Limits.prod.fst ≫ u) (Limits.prod.snd ≫ u) hab
  -- Hence `u ≫ F.map w` descends to a global section of `F k`.
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ :=
    exists_hom_terminal_of_prod_fst_comp_eq hKsurj (u := u ≫ F.map w)
      (by rwa [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc])
  have := hKsurj
  refine ⟨k, σ, (cancel_epi (terminal.from K)).1 ?_⟩
  rw [← Category.assoc, hσ, Category.assoc, colimit.w F w, hu]

end Main

private theorem injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_globalSections_proof {C : Type u}
    [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I] [IsFiltered I]
    [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)] (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :
    ((∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactTopos → Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactTopos →
        (∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      ((∃ S : Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v)),
          (∀ G : Sheaf J (Type max u v),
              Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G) →
                ∃ K ∈ S, Nonempty (K ⟶ G) ∧ Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K)) ∧
            ∀ K ∈ S, Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact (K ⨯ K)) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F (Sheaf.Γ J (Type max u v)))) :=
  ⟨injective_post_Γ_of_mono F, injective_post_Γ_of_isQuasiCompact F, fun hQC hmono =>
    ⟨injective_post_Γ_of_isQuasiCompact F hQC,
      surjective_post_Γ_of_exists F (exists_factor_of_isQuasiCompactTopos_of_mono F hQC hmono)⟩,
    bijective_post_Γ_of_covering_set F⟩

end

end Stacks.Sites.ColimitGlobalSections

namespace CategoryTheory.Sheaf

@[expose] public section

open Stacks.Sites.ColimitGlobalSections in
/-- **Stacks 0GMR.** Let `C` be a site and `F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)` a filtered diagram
of sheaves of sets. For the canonical map
`Ψ = colimit.post F (Γ J _) : colim_i Γ(C, F i) ⟶ Γ(C, colim_i F i)`:

1. if every transition map `F.map f` is a monomorphism, then `Ψ` is injective;
2. if the topos `Sh(C)` is quasi-compact (Stacks 0D07), then `Ψ` is injective;
3. if the topos `Sh(C)` is quasi-compact and every transition map is a monomorphism, then `Ψ`
   is bijective;
4. if there is a set `S` of sheaves such that every sheaf `G` surjecting onto the final sheaf
   admits a map `K ⟶ G` from some `K ∈ S` which itself surjects onto the final sheaf, and such
   that `K ⨯ K` is quasi-compact for every `K ∈ S`, then `Ψ` is bijective.

The four conjuncts are the four parts of the source, in order. -/
@[stacks 0GMR "Global sections of a filtered colimit of sheaves of sets.",
  sga "4 VI 1.23" "(i) qc⇒inj, X terminal"]
public theorem injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_globalSections {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {I : Type w₁} [Category.{w₂} I] [IsFiltered I]
    [HasColimitsOfShape I (Type max u v)] (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :
    ((∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactTopos → Function.Injective (colimit.post F (Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      (J.IsQuasiCompactTopos →
        (∀ (i j : I) (f : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map f)) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F (Γ J (Type max u v)))) ∧
      ((∃ S : Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v)),
          (∀ G : Sheaf J (Type max u v),
              IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G) →
                ∃ K ∈ S, Nonempty (K ⟶ G) ∧ IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K)) ∧
            ∀ K ∈ S, IsQuasiCompact (K ⨯ K)) →
        Function.Bijective (colimit.post F (Γ J (Type max u v)))) := by
  apply Stacks.Sites.ColimitGlobalSections.injective_and_bijective_colimit_post_globalSections_proof

/-- **Base change of a locally surjective morphism of sheaves of sets.**  If `G` surjects onto the
terminal sheaf, then the projection `prod.snd : G ⨯ K ⟶ K` is locally surjective for every sheaf
`K`: a section of `K` over `W` is paired, over the objects where `G` has a section, with such a
section.

Equivalently: the base change of the locally surjective `G ⟶ *` along `K ⟶ *` is locally
surjective.  This is the step used by Stacks 0GMR (4) and by Stacks 0GN3 to replace a sheaf
covering the final sheaf by a member of a given covering set. -/
public theorem isLocallySurjective_prod_snd {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {G K : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (hG : IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from G)) :
    IsLocallySurjective (Limits.prod.snd : G ⨯ K ⟶ K) := by
  apply Stacks.Sites.ColimitGlobalSections.isLocallySurjective_prod_snd hG

end

end CategoryTheory.Sheaf

